  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','Bathing every day helps to keep our body:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Clean"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Dirty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hungry"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bathing daily keeps the body clean."}',0.15,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','Which of these keeps our nails clean and healthy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutting them regularly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Leaving them long and dirty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Filling them with sand"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Painting them with mud"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cutting nails regularly keeps them clean and healthy."}',0.25,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','Eating fruits and vegetables helps our body to be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Strong and healthy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Weak and sick"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tired all day"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Always angry"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Fruits and vegetables help the body stay strong and healthy."}',0.25,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','Before crossing the road, you should look:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Left and right"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Only up"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only down"}, {"id": "d", "text": "With your eyes closed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "You should look left and right before crossing the road."}',0.2,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','Playing with a sharp knife at home can cause:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Injury"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Good health"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Happiness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cleaning"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Playing with a sharp knife can cause injury."}',0.2,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','You should cross a busy road using the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Zebra crossing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Middle of the road"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Gutter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rooftop"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A zebra crossing is a safe place to cross a busy road."}',0.3,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','To stay safe, children should not play with:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fire and matches"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A football"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A skipping rope"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A story book"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Children should not play with fire and matches because they are dangerous."}',0.2,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','When walking on a road with no pavement, you should walk:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Facing oncoming vehicles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "In the middle of the road"}, {"id": "c", "text": "With your back to all cars"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Lying on the road"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Walking facing oncoming vehicles helps you see and avoid them."}',0.35,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','The colours of the Nigerian flag are:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Green, white, green"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Red, white, blue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Black and yellow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Green and red"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Nigerian flag has green, white, green colours."}',0.25,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','The white colour on the Nigerian flag stands for:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Peace"}, {"id": "b", "text": "War"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Anger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The white colour on the flag stands for peace."}',0.3,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','The green colour on the Nigerian flag stands for:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Agriculture and rich land"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The sky"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Blood"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Darkness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The green colour stands for agriculture and Nigeria''s rich land."}',0.35,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','What do we sing to show love for our country Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The national anthem"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A birthday song"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A market song"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A play song"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We sing the national anthem to show love for our country."}',0.3,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','Which of these is a Nigerian national symbol?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The coat of arms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A football boot"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A school bag"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A market basket"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The coat of arms is a Nigerian national symbol."}',0.3,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','The capital city of Nigeria is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Abuja"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lagos"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Kano"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ibadan"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Abuja is the capital city of Nigeria."}',0.3,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','The people who live in Nigeria are called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nigerians"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ghanaians"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Americans"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Kenyans"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "People who live in Nigeria are called Nigerians."}',0.2,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','Nigeria is a country found in the continent of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Africa"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Europe"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Asia"}, {"id": "d", "text": "America"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Nigeria is a country in the continent of Africa."}',0.3,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','The three major languages spoken in Nigeria are Hausa, Igbo and:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "b", "text": "French"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Chinese"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Spanish"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The three major Nigerian languages are Hausa, Igbo and Yoruba."}',0.35,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P3','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','We should love our country Nigeria by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Obeying its laws and keeping it clean"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Destroying public property"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fighting one another"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Throwing rubbish everywhere"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We show love for Nigeria by obeying laws and keeping it clean."}',0.3,'{P3,SOS,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','What is agriculture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The growing of crops and rearing of animals for use by man"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The building of houses in the village"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The selling of clothes in the market"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The mending of roads in the city"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Agriculture is the growing of crops and rearing of animals for the use of man."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','The branch of agriculture that deals with the growing of crops is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "animal husbandry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "crop production"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fishery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "forestry"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Crop production is the branch of agriculture concerned with growing crops."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','The rearing of farm animals for man''s use is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "horticulture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "crop production"}, {"id": "c", "text": "animal husbandry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "agronomy"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Animal husbandry is the branch of agriculture that deals with rearing farm animals."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','The branch of agriculture concerned with the rearing of fish is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "poultry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fishery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "forestry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "piggery"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Fishery is the branch of agriculture that deals with the rearing of fish."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','A person who practises agriculture as an occupation is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "farmer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "trader"}, {"id": "c", "text": "driver"}, {"id": "d", "text": "tailor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A farmer is a person whose work is to grow crops or rear animals."}',0.25,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','One major importance of agriculture to man is that it provides','[{"id": "a", "text": "food"}, {"id": "b", "text": "electricity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "telephones"}, {"id": "d", "text": "aeroplanes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Agriculture provides food for people to eat."}',0.25,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','Agriculture provides raw materials such as cotton to which of these?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Textile industry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Motor mechanic"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Barber shop"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hospital"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cotton from farms is used as raw material by the textile industry to make cloth."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','Agriculture is important because it provides jobs and','[{"id": "a", "text": "income for farmers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "darkness at night"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flooding of towns"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sickness for people"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Farmers earn money (income) by selling their farm produce."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','Which of these farm products can be exported to earn money for Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cocoa"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nylon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cement"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cocoa is a Nigerian cash crop exported abroad to earn foreign money."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','Agriculture supplies materials like hides and skin used to make','[{"id": "a", "text": "shoes and bags"}, {"id": "b", "text": "glass windows"}, {"id": "c", "text": "iron nails"}, {"id": "d", "text": "plastic buckets"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hides and skin from animals are used to make leather shoes and bags."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','Which farm tool is used mainly for digging and making ridges?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hoe"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rake"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Watering can"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The hoe is used for digging the soil and making ridges."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','The farm tool used for clearing bushes and cutting grasses is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "cutlass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wheelbarrow"}, {"id": "c", "text": "watering can"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sieve"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The cutlass (matchet) is used for clearing bushes and cutting grasses."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','Which tool is used to water plants in the nursery?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watering can"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hoe"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Axe"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rake"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A watering can is used to sprinkle water on plants."}',0.25,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','The farm tool used for carrying loads such as manure around the farm is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "wheelbarrow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sickle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hoe"}, {"id": "d", "text": "spade"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A wheelbarrow is used to carry loads like manure and sand around the farm."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','Which of these tools is used for gathering leaves and grass together?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rake"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Watering can"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Knife"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A rake is used to gather dry leaves and grass together."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','To prevent farm tools made of metal from rusting, they should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "cleaned, dried and oiled after use"}, {"id": "b", "text": "left outside in the rain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "buried in wet soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kept inside water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cleaning, drying and oiling metal tools after use prevents rust."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','A blunt cutlass should be made sharp again by','[{"id": "a", "text": "sharpening it with a file or stone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "soaking it in water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "burning it in fire"}, {"id": "d", "text": "throwing it away"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A blunt cutlass is sharpened with a file or sharpening stone."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','Farm tools should be kept in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "dry store or tool shed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pool of water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "open bush"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cooking pot"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tools are stored in a dry store or shed to keep them safe and rust-free."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','Reddish-brown coating that forms on wet metal tools is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "rust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "paint"}, {"id": "c", "text": "oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "grease"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Rust is the reddish-brown coating that forms when metal is left wet."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','The best reason for caring for farm tools is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make them last longer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "make them heavier"}, {"id": "c", "text": "change their colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make them rust faster"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Proper care makes farm tools last longer and remain useful."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Crops that are grown mainly to be eaten as food are called','[{"id": "a", "text": "food crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "weeds"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flowers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "shade crops"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Food crops are grown mainly to provide food for people."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Cocoa, rubber and cotton are examples of','[{"id": "a", "text": "cash crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "food crops"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weeds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vegetables"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cash crops such as cocoa, rubber and cotton are grown mainly to be sold."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Which of these is a grain (cereal) crop?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Maize"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Yam"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cassava"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Orange"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Maize is a cereal (grain) crop."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Yam and cassava are grouped as','[{"id": "a", "text": "root and tuber crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cereal crops"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fruit crops"}, {"id": "d", "text": "beverage crops"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Yam and cassava are root and tuber crops because we eat their underground parts."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','A crop that completes its life cycle within one year is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "an annual crop"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a perennial crop"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a cash crop"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a weed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Annual crops grow, produce and die within one year."}',0.45,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','The first step in preparing a piece of land for planting is','[{"id": "a", "text": "clearing the land"}, {"id": "b", "text": "harvesting the crop"}, {"id": "c", "text": "storing the produce"}, {"id": "d", "text": "selling the crop"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Land is first cleared of bushes before planting can begin."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','The planting of seeds or seedlings in the soil is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "sowing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "weeding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "harvesting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "storage"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sowing is the placing of seeds or seedlings into the soil."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','Removing unwanted plants that grow among crops is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "weeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "planting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "clearing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "watering"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weeding is the removal of weeds growing among the crops."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','The gathering of matured crops from the farm is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "harvesting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sowing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "clearing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Harvesting is the gathering of crops that are ready or mature."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','Adding manure or fertilizer to the soil helps the crop by','[{"id": "a", "text": "supplying food nutrients for growth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "killing the crop"}, {"id": "c", "text": "drying the soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bringing weeds"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Manure and fertilizer add nutrients that help crops grow well."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','Which of these farm animals gives us eggs?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fowl"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Goat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sheep"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Fowls (hens) lay eggs that we eat."}',0.25,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','We get milk mainly from the','[{"id": "a", "text": "cow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fowl"}, {"id": "c", "text": "duck"}, {"id": "d", "text": "turkey"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cows are reared to give us milk."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','Which farm animal is kept mainly for its wool?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sheep"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fowl"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rabbit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pig"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sheep give us wool used for making warm clothing."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','The rearing of fowls, ducks and turkeys is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "poultry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "piggery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fishery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "apiary"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Poultry is the rearing of birds like fowls, ducks and turkeys."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','Which farm animal is kept mainly to provide pork as meat?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pig"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cow"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Goat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sheep"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The pig provides pork, which is the meat we get from it."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','The house built to keep fowls is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "poultry house"}, {"id": "b", "text": "kennel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "barn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "silo"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A poultry house is where fowls are kept and cared for."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','Farm animals must be given clean water so that they will','[{"id": "a", "text": "stay healthy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fall sick"}, {"id": "c", "text": "run away"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stop eating"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clean water keeps farm animals healthy."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','Sick farm animals should be treated by giving them','[{"id": "a", "text": "medicine or drugs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "more mud"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dirty water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "no food at all"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sick animals are treated with medicine or drugs to make them well."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','The food given to farm animals is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "feed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "manure"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fertilizer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "weed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Feed is the food given to farm animals to help them grow."}',0.35,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','The animal house of farm animals should be kept','[{"id": "a", "text": "clean and dry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wet and dirty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "full of mud"}, {"id": "d", "text": "flooded with water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clean and dry animal house keeps the animals healthy and free from disease."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','The three main types of soil are sandy soil, clay soil and','[{"id": "a", "text": "loamy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rocky soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wet soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "black soil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The three main soil types are sandy, clay and loamy soil."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','Which type of soil is the best for growing most crops?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Loamy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sandy soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Clay soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rocky soil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Loamy soil is the best for crops because it holds water and has plenty of nutrients."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','The soil that feels rough and allows water to drain away quickly is','[{"id": "a", "text": "sandy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "clay soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "loamy soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "humus"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sandy soil feels rough and drains water quickly because its particles are large."}',0.45,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','The soil that is sticky when wet and holds a lot of water is','[{"id": "a", "text": "clay soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sandy soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "loamy soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "gravel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clay soil is sticky when wet and holds much water because its particles are very fine."}',0.45,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','The dark, decayed remains of plants and animals in the soil is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "humus"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gravel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stone"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Humus is the dark, decayed remains of plants and animals that makes soil fertile."}',0.45,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','Land is important to the farmer because it provides a place to','[{"id": "a", "text": "grow crops and rear animals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sail boats"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fly aeroplanes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "swim in the sea"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Land gives the farmer a place to grow crops and keep animals."}',0.3,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','The soil is important to plants because it holds the roots and supplies','[{"id": "a", "text": "water and nutrients"}, {"id": "b", "text": "electricity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "petrol"}, {"id": "d", "text": "plastic"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Soil holds plant roots firmly and supplies water and nutrients for growth."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','Soil that has many nutrients for plant growth is said to be','[{"id": "a", "text": "fertile"}, {"id": "b", "text": "poor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hard"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A fertile soil is rich in nutrients that help plants grow well."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','The washing away of the top soil by water or wind is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "soil erosion"}, {"id": "b", "text": "harvesting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "planting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Soil erosion is the carrying away of top soil by water or wind."}',0.45,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','One good way a farmer can keep the soil fertile is by adding','[{"id": "a", "text": "manure to the soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nylon to the soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "broken bottles to the soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "petrol to the soil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Adding manure returns nutrients to the soil and keeps it fertile."}',0.4,'{P4,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','Which of these is a basic element of art used when drawing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Line"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Song"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Drum"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A line is one of the basic elements of art used to make drawings."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','The colours red, blue and yellow are called what type of colours?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Secondary colours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Primary colours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Neutral colours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Shades"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Red, blue and yellow are the three primary colours from which others are made."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','What do you get when you mix the primary colours blue and yellow?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Purple"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Orange"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Green"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Brown"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Mixing blue and yellow produces the secondary colour green."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','The roughness or smoothness of a surface in art is known as its what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Texture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Shape"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rhythm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Volume"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Texture is the element of art that describes how a surface feels or looks."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','A round, closed line that has no beginning or end forms which shape?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Triangle"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Square"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rectangle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Circle"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "A closed curved line with no corners forms a circle."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','Which tool is most suitable for painting a wide area with colour?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Brush"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ruler"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Eraser"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Scissors"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A brush is used to spread paint over a surface when painting."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','What is a pencil mainly used for in art?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutting paper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Drawing and sketching"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mixing water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Gluing shapes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A pencil is used for drawing lines and making sketches."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','Which material is added to powder or cake paint to make it flow before painting?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Salt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Chalk"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Water is mixed with paint to make it flow smoothly onto the surface."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','What is the correct thing to do with your brush after painting?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Break it in two"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Leave paint to dry on it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wash it clean and keep it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Throw it away"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Brushes should be washed clean and stored so they can be reused."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','Which of these is the best surface for a pupil to paint on in class?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Drawing paper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A glass window"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The classroom floor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A friend''s shirt"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Drawing paper is the proper surface for classroom painting work."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Which craft involves weaving raffia or cane to make baskets and mats?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Weaving"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Carving"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Painting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Singing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weaving is the craft of interlacing materials like raffia or cane into baskets and mats."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','A clay pot is made using which local craft?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Dyeing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pottery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Embroidery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Beading"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pottery is the craft of moulding clay into pots and other objects."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Which material is mainly used by a wood carver to make a stool?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wood"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clay"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cloth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Glass"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Wood carving uses wood as its main material to make items like stools."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','The Yoruba tie-and-dye cloth known for its blue colour is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Akwete"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Adire"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Aso-oke"}, {"id": "d", "text": "George"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Adire is the Yoruba tie-and-dye cloth traditionally dyed with indigo (blue)."}',0.45,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Bags and necklaces made by threading small colourful beads is called what craft?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bead work"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pottery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Carving"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Weaving"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bead work is the craft of threading beads to make ornaments and bags."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','A woven raffia basket is mainly used for what purpose in the home?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Storing and carrying things"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cooking food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Lighting the room"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Washing clothes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Baskets are used for storing and carrying items such as food and clothes."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','How do local crafts help people in the community earn a living?','[{"id": "a", "text": "By selling the crafts for money"}, {"id": "b", "text": "By hiding them at home"}, {"id": "c", "text": "By burning them"}, {"id": "d", "text": "By giving them all away free"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Craftsmen earn income by selling the items they make."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','A clay water pot is useful in many Nigerian homes because it helps to do what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Keep drinking water cool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Boil water quickly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Give out light"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Play music"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clay pots keep stored water cool, which is why they are valued in homes."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','Why are local crafts important to our Nigerian culture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "They preserve and show our tradition"}, {"id": "b", "text": "They replace our food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "They stop people from working"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They make the weather change"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Local crafts help preserve and display the traditions of our people."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','A carved wooden mortar (odo) is used in the home to do what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pound food such as yam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Store water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sweep the floor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sew clothes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A wooden mortar is used with a pestle to pound food like yam."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','The talking drum (gangan) is played by doing what to it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Blowing into it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Beating it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Plucking its strings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Shaking water in it"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The talking drum is a percussion instrument that is played by beating."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','The flute is an instrument that is played by doing what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Blowing air into it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Beating it with a stick"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shaking it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rubbing it on the ground"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A flute is a wind instrument sounded by blowing air into it."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','The sekere (shaker made from a gourd and beads) makes sound when you do what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Blow it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Shake it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Read it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bury it"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The sekere is a shaker that produces sound when shaken."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','The goje, a Nigerian instrument played with a bow across a string, is which type of instrument?','[{"id": "a", "text": "String instrument"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wind instrument"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Percussion instrument"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Electronic instrument"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The goje has strings and is a string (stringed) instrument."}',0.45,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','Which of these instruments belongs to the percussion (beaten) family?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Flute"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Trumpet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Drum"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Harmonica"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A drum is a percussion instrument because it is played by beating."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','In music, a steady beat that you can clap or tap along to is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rhythm"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shape"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Texture"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Rhythm is the pattern of beats you clap or tap in music."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','The signs written to show musical sounds on lines and spaces are called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Letters"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Notes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Numbers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Drums"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Musical sounds are written using notes."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','The sol-fa notes doh, re, mi, fa, sol, la, ti, doh are used mainly for what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Singing melodies"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Drawing pictures"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Counting money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Weaving mats"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The sol-fa syllables are used to sing the notes of a melody."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','When we clap once for every beat of a song, we are keeping the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Silence"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Beat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Paint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Costume"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clapping once for each pulse means we are keeping the beat."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','A short period of no sound in music is called a what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Beat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Line"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Drum"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A rest is a moment of silence in music."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','The Atilogwu dance with acrobatic display comes from which Nigerian people?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Efik"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tiv"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Atilogwu is a lively acrobatic dance of the Igbo people."}',0.45,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','A dance performed to celebrate a new king or important event is best described as what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A ceremonial dance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A quarrel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A lesson note"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A painting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Dances done for celebrations and events are ceremonial dances."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','Which of these is usually needed to guide the steps of a traditional dance?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Music from drums"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A cooking pot"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A school bell only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A pencil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Drum music provides the rhythm that guides dancers'' steps."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','Colourful clothes and beads worn by dancers during a performance are called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Costumes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Textbooks"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tools"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Baskets"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The special outfits worn by dancers are called costumes."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','The Sharo/Shadi and Koroso dances are commonly performed among which people?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hausa/Fulani"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ijaw"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Igbo"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Koroso and related dances are associated with the Hausa/Fulani of northern Nigeria."}',0.45,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','A person who acts a part in a play or drama is called a what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Actor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Farmer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Driver"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tailor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An actor is a person who plays a role in a drama."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','In drama, the words that an actor says are known as the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Dialogue"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Costume"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Curtain"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Dialogue is the spoken words exchanged by actors in a drama."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','The place where actors perform a play before the audience is called the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Market"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Kitchen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Farm"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The stage is the area where actors perform a play."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','The people who watch a drama being performed are called the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Audience"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Actors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Directors"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Dancers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The audience is the group of people who watch a performance."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','When pupils pretend to be different people to act out a story, they are doing a what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Role play"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spelling test"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Football match"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Drawing lesson"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Acting out a story by pretending to be others is called role play."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','The art of folding paper into shapes such as boats and hats is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Paper folding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pottery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dyeing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Carving"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Making shapes by folding paper is called paper folding."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','Which tool is used to cut paper neatly into shapes?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Scissors"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spoon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hammer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Comb"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Scissors are used to cut paper cleanly into shapes."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','What is used to join two pieces of paper together in paper craft?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Gum or glue"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Water only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Salt"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Gum or glue is used to stick pieces of paper together."}',0.3,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','Sticking small pieces of coloured paper onto a surface to form a picture is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Collage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Weaving"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pottery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Singing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A collage is made by pasting pieces of paper or material to form a picture."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','A paper lantern is best made from which kind of material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Coloured paper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wet clay"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Iron rod"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Broken glass"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Paper lanterns are made by cutting and folding coloured paper."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','Tie-and-dye is a method of decorating what kind of material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cloth or fabric"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wood"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Metal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stone"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tie-and-dye is used to add colour and patterns to cloth (fabric)."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','In tie-and-dye, why do we tie parts of the cloth with thread before dyeing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "So those parts do not take the dye and form patterns"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To make the cloth heavier"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To cook the cloth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To keep the cloth dry forever"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tied areas resist the dye, leaving patterns on the cloth."}',0.45,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','The coloured liquid used to change the colour of cloth in tie-and-dye is called the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Dye"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Glue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ink pen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clay"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Dye is the coloured liquid used to colour the cloth."}',0.35,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','Which local Nigerian colour plant is traditionally used to dye adire cloth blue?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Indigo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cassava"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Maize"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pepper"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Indigo (elu) is the plant traditionally used to dye adire cloth blue."}',0.45,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','Sewing coloured threads to make designs and pictures on cloth is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Embroidery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Carving"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Painting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pottery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Embroidery is decorating cloth with designs made from stitched thread."}',0.4,'{P4,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','What do we mean by values in Civic Education?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Toys that children play with"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Things that are important and accepted as good in a society"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Money kept in a bank"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Names of towns and cities"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Values are the good qualities and beliefs that a society accepts as important and worthy."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','Which of the following is a good value that people should have?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stealing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lying"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Honesty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cheating"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Honesty is a good value because it means being truthful and trustworthy."}',0.25,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','Values help us to know the difference between what is right and what is _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "wrong"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sweet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "far"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Values guide us to tell the difference between right and wrong behaviour."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','A pupil who returns money found in the school compound to the owner is showing the value of _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "greed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "honesty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "anger"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Returning found money to its owner shows honesty and truthfulness."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','Which of these is NOT a good value?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Kindness"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Obedience"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Selfishness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Discipline"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Selfishness is a bad value because it means caring only about oneself."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','The value of always keeping to time and doing things when they should be done is called _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "punctuality"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rudeness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "greed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pride"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Punctuality means being on time and doing things at the right time."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','Showing love and helping people who are in need is the value of _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "wickedness"}, {"id": "b", "text": "kindness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "jealousy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "laziness"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Kindness means being caring and helpful to other people."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','Why are good values important in our society?','[{"id": "a", "text": "They cause fighting and quarrels"}, {"id": "b", "text": "They make people poor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "They help people live together in peace"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They make children sleep in class"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Good values help people to live together peacefully and happily."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','A child who does his or her work well without being forced is showing _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "hard work"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cheating"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stealing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fear"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hard work means doing your duties diligently without being forced."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','Respecting elders and obeying good rules shows the value of _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "disobedience"}, {"id": "b", "text": "respect"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pride"}, {"id": "d", "text": "greed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Respect means honouring elders and obeying good rules and laws."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','Honesty means being _______ at all times.','[{"id": "a", "text": "truthful"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wicked"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lazy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "proud"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Honesty means being truthful and sincere in what we say and do."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','A pupil who tells the teacher the truth about who broke the window is being _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "dishonest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "honest"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rude"}, {"id": "d", "text": "greedy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Telling the truth even when it is hard shows honesty."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','Which of the following is an example of dishonesty?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Telling the truth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cheating in an examination"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Returning a borrowed pen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Keeping a promise"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cheating in an examination is a form of dishonesty and unfairness."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','A trader who gives the correct change to a customer is showing _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "honesty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hatred"}, {"id": "c", "text": "anger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fear"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Giving the correct change shows the trader is honest and trustworthy."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','Keeping the promises we make to others is a form of _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "greed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "honesty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pride"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Keeping promises shows that a person is honest and reliable."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','One benefit of being honest is that people will _______ you.','[{"id": "a", "text": "trust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hate"}, {"id": "c", "text": "beat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fear"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Honest people are trusted because others believe what they say."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','An honest worker in an office is likely to be _______ by the boss.','[{"id": "a", "text": "sacked"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rewarded"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hated"}, {"id": "d", "text": "punished"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An honest worker earns trust and is often rewarded for good conduct."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','Which of these is a result of dishonesty?','[{"id": "a", "text": "People trust you"}, {"id": "b", "text": "You are loved by all"}, {"id": "c", "text": "You lose the trust of others"}, {"id": "d", "text": "You are given awards"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Dishonesty makes people lose trust and confidence in a person."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','Honesty helps a society to grow because it reduces _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "peace"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stealing and cheating"}, {"id": "c", "text": "love"}, {"id": "d", "text": "unity"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "When people are honest, there is less stealing and cheating in society."}',0.4,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','A student known for honesty will always have a good _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "name"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sickness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "quarrel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "punishment"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An honest person earns a good name and reputation among people."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','Cooperation means _______ together to do a task.','[{"id": "a", "text": "fighting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "working"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sleeping"}, {"id": "d", "text": "quarreling"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cooperation means people working together to achieve a common goal."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','Which of these is an example of cooperation in the school?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pupils cleaning the classroom together"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A pupil fighting another pupil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A pupil refusing to share"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A pupil sleeping in class"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Pupils cleaning the classroom together is an example of cooperation."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','When members of a family help one another with house chores, they are showing _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "cooperation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "selfishness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hatred"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Helping one another with chores at home is a form of cooperation."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','A group of people working together is often called a _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "team"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prison"}, {"id": "c", "text": "market"}, {"id": "d", "text": "river"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A group of people cooperating on a task is called a team."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','In a football match, players must _______ to win.','[{"id": "a", "text": "cooperate"}, {"id": "b", "text": "quarrel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "run away"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fight the referee"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Football players must cooperate as a team in order to win a match."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','Cooperation makes difficult work become _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "harder"}, {"id": "b", "text": "easier"}, {"id": "c", "text": "impossible"}, {"id": "d", "text": "longer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "When people cooperate, hard work becomes easier and faster to finish."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','When people in a community clear the road together, this is called _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "communal labour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stealing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fighting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "trading"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "People joining to clear the road together is called communal labour, a form of cooperation."}',0.4,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','One good result of cooperation in a community is _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "war"}, {"id": "b", "text": "progress and development"}, {"id": "c", "text": "poverty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hunger"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cooperation brings progress and development to a community."}',0.4,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','Cooperation among people brings about peace and _______ in society.','[{"id": "a", "text": "unity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "trouble"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sickness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "quarrel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cooperation promotes peace and unity among people in a society."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','Which of these shows the importance of cooperation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Work is finished quickly when people help one another"}, {"id": "b", "text": "People become enemies"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nothing gets done"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Everyone works alone slowly"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cooperation helps work to be finished quickly when people help each other."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','How many colours does the Nigerian national flag have?','[{"id": "a", "text": "One"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Two"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Three"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Four"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Nigerian flag has two colours: green and white."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','The green colour on the Nigerian flag stands for _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "peace and unity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "agriculture and rich land"}, {"id": "c", "text": "blood and war"}, {"id": "d", "text": "gold and money"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The green colour represents Nigeria''s agriculture and rich, fertile land."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','The white colour on the Nigerian flag stands for _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "war"}, {"id": "b", "text": "peace and unity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "farming"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hunger"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The white colour on the flag represents peace and unity."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','Which of these is a national symbol of Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The Coat of Arms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A market stall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A football boot"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A school bag"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Coat of Arms is one of Nigeria''s national symbols."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','The national flag of Nigeria was designed by _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nnamdi Azikiwe"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Taiwo Akinkunmi"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Herbert Macaulay"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tafawa Balewa"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Nigerian flag was designed by Taiwo Akinkunmi in 1959."}',0.45,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','The eagle on the Nigerian Coat of Arms stands for _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "weakness"}, {"id": "b", "text": "strength"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hunger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sickness"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The eagle on the Coat of Arms represents strength."}',0.4,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','The two white horses on the Coat of Arms stand for _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "dignity and pride"}, {"id": "b", "text": "war and fighting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "food and water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "money and gold"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The two horses on the Coat of Arms stand for dignity and pride."}',0.45,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','We should show respect to national symbols because they represent our _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "country"}, {"id": "b", "text": "toys"}, {"id": "c", "text": "food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "clothes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "National symbols represent our country, so we must respect them."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','When the National Anthem is being sung, we should _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "stand at attention"}, {"id": "b", "text": "run about"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sit and eat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sleep"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We should stand at attention to show respect when the National Anthem is sung."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','The National Pledge is a promise we make to be _______ to our country.','[{"id": "a", "text": "faithful and loyal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wicked"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lazy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dishonest"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The National Pledge is a promise to be faithful, loyal and honest to Nigeria."}',0.4,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','One important duty of a good citizen is to obey the _______ of the country.','[{"id": "a", "text": "laws"}, {"id": "b", "text": "toys"}, {"id": "c", "text": "songs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "trees"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A good citizen has a duty to obey the laws of the country."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','Adult citizens have the duty to pay _______ to the government.','[{"id": "a", "text": "tax"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "grass"}, {"id": "d", "text": "leaves"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Paying tax is a duty of adult citizens to help the government run the country."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','Which of these is a duty of a good citizen?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Destroying public property"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Protecting public property"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fighting the police"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Refusing to obey rules"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Protecting public property is one of the duties of a good citizen."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','A good citizen keeps the environment _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "dirty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "clean"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flooded"}, {"id": "d", "text": "noisy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A good citizen keeps the environment clean and tidy."}',0.3,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','During election, adult citizens have the duty to _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "vote"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sleep at home"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "travel abroad"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Adult citizens have a duty to vote and choose good leaders during elections."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','When citizens obey the law, the country enjoys _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "peace and order"}, {"id": "b", "text": "war"}, {"id": "c", "text": "confusion"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hunger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Obeying the law brings peace and order to the country."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','The tax paid by citizens is used by the government to build _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "schools and roads"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nothing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "toys"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cartoons"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The government uses tax to build schools, roads, hospitals and other amenities."}',0.4,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','If citizens refuse to perform their duties, the country will not _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "develop"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sleep"}, {"id": "d", "text": "eat"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A country cannot develop well if citizens refuse to perform their duties."}',0.4,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','A citizen who reports crime to the police is helping to keep the community _______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "safe"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dirty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hungry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "poor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Reporting crime to the police helps to keep the community safe and secure."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','Performing our duties as citizens shows that we _______ our country.','[{"id": "a", "text": "love"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hate"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fear"}, {"id": "d", "text": "forget"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Performing our duties shows that we love and care for our country."}',0.35,'{P4,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','According to the book of Genesis, how many days did God take to create the world before He rested?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Five days"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Six days"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Seven days"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Three days"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "God created everything in six days and rested on the seventh day."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','What did God create on the very first day of creation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Light"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fish"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Human beings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Trees"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "On the first day God said, ''Let there be light,'' and there was light."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','On which day of creation did God make the sun, moon and stars?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The second day"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The third day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The fourth day"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The first day"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "God made the sun, moon and stars on the fourth day of creation."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','What did God do on the seventh day of creation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "He created the animals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "He rested from His work"}, {"id": "c", "text": "He made the sea"}, {"id": "d", "text": "He created man"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "God rested on the seventh day, making it a holy day of rest."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','The first man that God created was named:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Noah"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Abraham"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Adam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Moses"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "God created the first man and named him Adam."}',0.25,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','Which of these actions shows that we are caring for God''s creation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Throwing rubbish into the river"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Planting and watering trees"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Killing animals for fun"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Burning the bush carelessly"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Planting and watering trees helps to protect and care for God''s creation."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','God gave human beings the responsibility to do what with His creation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To take care of it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To destroy it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To waste it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To ignore it"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God asked human beings to take care of and rule over His creation wisely."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','Keeping our school compound clean is a way of showing that we:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Do not like our teachers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Care for God''s world"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Are wasting our time"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Want to leave school"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Keeping our surroundings clean shows that we care for the world God made."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','Which of these is a good way to care for animals God created?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Beating them cruelly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Feeding and sheltering them"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Starving them"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Chasing them away with stones"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Feeding and giving shelter to animals is a kind way to care for them."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','Wasting clean water carelessly is wrong because water is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "A useless thing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A gift from God we should value"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only for washing cars"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bad for our health"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Water is a precious gift from God, so we should use it wisely and not waste it."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','From which city did God call Abraham to leave and go to a new land?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Jerusalem"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ur"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Egypt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Babylon"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "God called Abraham to leave Ur and journey to the land He would show him."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','What was the name of Abraham''s wife who travelled with him?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rebecca"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rachel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sarah"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leah"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Sarah was Abraham''s wife who journeyed with him to the promised land."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','When God called Abraham, He asked him to leave his country and his:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Father''s household"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sheep and cattle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Clothes and food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Money and gold"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God told Abraham to leave his country and his father''s household for a new land."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','Abraham obeyed God''s call because he had:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fear of the people"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Faith and trust in God"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nowhere else to go"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A wish to become rich"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Abraham obeyed because he had faith and trusted that God would keep His word."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','The land that God promised to give Abraham and his children was:','[{"id": "a", "text": "The land of Canaan"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The land of Egypt"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The land of Persia"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The land of Greece"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God promised to give Abraham the land of Canaan."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','The main lesson we learn from the way Abraham answered God''s call is that we should:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Obey God even when it is hard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Argue with God"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wait for many years before obeying"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Only obey when we are rewarded"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Abraham teaches us to obey God even when what He asks is difficult."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','God promised to bless Abraham and make his descendants as many as the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fishes in the pond"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Stars in the sky"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stones on the road"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leaves on one tree"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "God promised Abraham descendants as numerous as the stars in the sky."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','A child who obeys his parents quickly is showing the same virtue that Abraham showed, which is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Greed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Obedience"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pride"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Laziness"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Like Abraham, an obedient child listens and does what is asked without delay."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','Because Abraham believed God''s promise even before it came true, we learn to have:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Doubt"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Faith"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Anger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fear"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Abraham''s trust in God''s unseen promise is an example of true faith."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','Abraham is often called the ''father of faith'' because he:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Was very rich"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Trusted and obeyed God fully"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Built the biggest house"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Had many servants"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "He is called the father of faith because of his complete trust and obedience to God."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','In which town was Jesus Christ born?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nazareth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bethlehem"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Jerusalem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Jericho"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea, as the Bible records."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','What was the name of the mother of Jesus?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Martha"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Elizabeth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mary"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ruth"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Mary was the mother of Jesus Christ."}',0.25,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','After Jesus was born, He was laid in a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Golden bed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Manger"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Basket of reeds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wooden boat"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Baby Jesus was laid in a manger because there was no room in the inn."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','Who were the first people told about the birth of Jesus by the angels?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The kings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The shepherds"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The soldiers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The teachers of the law"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Angels announced the good news of Jesus'' birth to shepherds in the fields."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','The wise men from the east followed a special sign to find Jesus. The sign was a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bright star"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Loud trumpet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Flowing river"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tall mountain"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The wise men followed a bright star that led them to the baby Jesus."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','How many kinds of gifts did the wise men bring to baby Jesus?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Two"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Three"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Four"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Five"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The wise men brought three gifts: gold, frankincense and myrrh."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','Which of these was one of the gifts the wise men gave to Jesus?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Silver"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Gold"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bronze"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Diamond"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The wise men presented gold, frankincense and myrrh to Jesus."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','As a boy of twelve, where was Jesus found sitting among the teachers?','[{"id": "a", "text": "In the temple"}, {"id": "b", "text": "In the market"}, {"id": "c", "text": "By the seaside"}, {"id": "d", "text": "In a garden"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The boy Jesus was found in the temple listening to and questioning the teachers."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','When Jesus stayed behind in the temple, the teachers were amazed at His:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fine clothes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wisdom and understanding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Loud singing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Big size"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The teachers were amazed at the wisdom and understanding of the young Jesus."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','The story of the boy Jesus in the temple teaches children to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Avoid the house of God"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Love learning about God"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Disobey their parents"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Play all day long"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus in the temple shows children to be eager to learn about God."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','At a wedding in Cana, Jesus turned water into:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Oil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wine"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Milk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Honey"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus'' first miracle was turning water into wine at the wedding in Cana."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','Jesus fed a large crowd with five loaves of bread and two:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Eggs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fishes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Oranges"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cups of water"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus fed the crowd with five loaves and two fishes."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','When a storm arose on the sea, Jesus calmed it by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rowing the boat faster"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Commanding the wind and waves to be still"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Swimming to the shore"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Jumping into the water"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus commanded the wind and the waves, and the storm became calm."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','Jesus showed His power over sickness when He healed people who were:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sad and lonely"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blind and lame"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rich and proud"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tall and strong"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus healed many who were blind, lame and sick, showing His power over sickness."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','The miracles of Jesus show us that He is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "An ordinary man"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The powerful Son of God"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A great trader"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A famous king of Egypt"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The miracles reveal that Jesus is the powerful Son of God."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','In the parable of the Good Samaritan, who stopped to help the wounded man?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The priest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The Levite"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The Samaritan"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The rich merchant"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The Good Samaritan was the one who stopped and cared for the wounded man."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','The main lesson of the parable of the Good Samaritan is that we should:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Help only our friends"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Help anyone who is in need"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pass by people in trouble"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Help only rich people"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The parable teaches us to show kindness and help anyone in need."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','In the parable of the Lost Sheep, the shepherd left the ninety-nine to look for the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "One that was lost"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Biggest sheep"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Youngest lamb"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sick goat"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The shepherd searched for the one lost sheep, showing God''s care for everyone."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','The parable of the Prodigal Son teaches us about God''s:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Anger"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Forgiveness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wealth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Punishment"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The father''s welcome of his lost son shows God''s readiness to forgive."}',0.4,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','Jesus taught many lessons using simple stories called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Parables"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Songs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Poems"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Riddles"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jesus used parables, which are simple stories that teach moral lessons."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','The special prayer that Jesus taught His disciples is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Lord''s Prayer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Morning song"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grace before meals"}, {"id": "d", "text": "National anthem"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jesus taught His disciples the Lord''s Prayer, beginning ''Our Father in heaven''."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','Prayer is best described as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Talking with God"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reading a story book"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Playing with friends"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Singing for money"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Prayer is the way Christians talk with and listen to God."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','Before eating our food, it is good for Christians to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Shout loudly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Say a prayer of thanks"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Quarrel with others"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Run outside"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Christians thank God in prayer for the food He provides."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','The Lord''s Prayer begins with the words:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Our Father in heaven"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Thank you for today"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bless this food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Good morning Lord"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Lord''s Prayer opens with ''Our Father in heaven, hallowed be your name''."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','We can pray to God:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Only inside a church"}, {"id": "b", "text": "At any time and in any place"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only on Christmas day"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Only when we are sad"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Christians can pray to God at any time and in any place."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','A pupil who finds money on the floor and returns it to the owner is being:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Honest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Greedy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Lazy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rude"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Returning what does not belong to you is an act of honesty."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','The Bible teaches Christians to love their neighbours as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Themselves"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Their enemies"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Strangers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Their money"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jesus taught, ''Love your neighbour as yourself''."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','Which of these actions shows kindness to others?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Helping a blind man cross the road"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Laughing at a poor child"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Refusing to share your food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fighting your classmates"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Helping a blind man cross the road is a clear act of kindness."}',0.3,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','Telling lies is against Christian teaching because God wants us to be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Truthful"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Boastful"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Selfish"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Careless"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God wants Christians to be truthful and to avoid telling lies."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','A child who obeys his parents and teachers is keeping God''s command to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Honour father and mother"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sleep all day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Win every game"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Eat plenty of food"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Obeying parents and teachers keeps the command to honour your father and mother."}',0.35,'{P4,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Home Economics is best described as the study of how to manage and care for the home and the ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "market"}, {"id": "b", "text": "family"}, {"id": "c", "text": "school"}, {"id": "d", "text": "farm"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Home Economics teaches how to care for the home and the well-being of the family."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Which of these is a main reason we study Home Economics in school?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To learn how to keep the home and family healthy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To learn how to drive a car"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To learn how to build houses"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To learn how to trade shares"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Home Economics helps us care for the home and keep the family healthy."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','A pupil who has learnt Home Economics is MOST likely to know how to ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "repair a mobile phone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prepare a simple balanced meal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "solve algebra equations"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fix a car engine"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Preparing simple meals for the family is a basic Home Economics skill."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Home Economics helps a family to spend its money wisely. This is an example of good ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "quarrelling"}, {"id": "b", "text": "management"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wasting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "borrowing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Spending money wisely is part of good home management."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Which statement about Home Economics is TRUE?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It is only useful for girls"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It is useful for both boys and girls"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It is only useful for adults"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It has no use at home"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Home Economics skills are useful for everyone, both boys and girls."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','Which of these is one of the main areas of Home Economics?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Foods and nutrition"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Football coaching"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Music production"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Road building"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Foods and nutrition is one of the main areas studied in Home Economics."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','Learning how to sew, wash and iron clothes belongs to the Home Economics area called ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "clothing and textiles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "child development"}, {"id": "c", "text": "home management"}, {"id": "d", "text": "foods and nutrition"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sewing, washing and ironing clothes fall under clothing and textiles."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','Taking care of a baby and helping children grow well is part of which area of Home Economics?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Clothing and textiles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Child development and care"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Foods and nutrition"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Laundry"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Caring for babies and children is part of child development and care."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','Keeping the house clean, arranging furniture and managing family money is part of ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "home management"}, {"id": "b", "text": "foods and nutrition"}, {"id": "c", "text": "clothing and textiles"}, {"id": "d", "text": "farming"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cleaning, arranging and managing family resources belong to home management."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','Which pair below are BOTH areas of Home Economics?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Foods and nutrition, clothing and textiles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Football, swimming"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Trading, banking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Driving, welding"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Foods and nutrition and clothing and textiles are both areas of Home Economics."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','How many times a day should you brush your teeth to keep them clean and healthy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Once every week"}, {"id": "b", "text": "At least twice a day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only when they hurt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Once every month"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Teeth should be brushed at least twice daily, morning and night."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','You should wash your hands with soap and water especially ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "after using the toilet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "only on Sundays"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only when they look dirty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "once a week"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hands should be washed with soap after using the toilet to remove germs."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','Which item is used together with water to clean the body during a bath?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Soap"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Petrol"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Chalk"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Soap and water are used together to wash the body clean."}',0.25,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','Keeping the fingernails short and clean helps to ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "stop germs and dirt from hiding under them"}, {"id": "b", "text": "make the hands weak"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make you fall sick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "help germs to grow"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Short, clean nails leave no place for germs and dirt to hide."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','Bathing at least twice a day in a hot climate like Nigeria mainly helps to ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "remove sweat and body odour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "make the body dirty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "waste soap and water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "damage the skin"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bathing removes sweat and body odour, keeping the skin fresh and clean."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','Which item is used to comb and neaten the hair?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A spoon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A ruler"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A cup"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A comb is used to make the hair tidy and neat."}',0.25,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','A toothbrush and toothpaste are used to clean the ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "teeth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "feet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "clothes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A toothbrush and toothpaste are used to clean the teeth."}',0.25,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','Which item is used to cut the fingernails and toenails?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nail clipper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sponge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Towel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Comb"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A nail clipper is used to trim the fingernails and toenails."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','After a bath, you use a clean ______ to dry your body.','[{"id": "a", "text": "towel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "plate"}, {"id": "c", "text": "shoe"}, {"id": "d", "text": "book"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clean towel is used to dry the body after bathing."}',0.25,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','A sponge is mainly used during a bath to ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "scrub and clean the skin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "comb the hair"}, {"id": "c", "text": "brush the teeth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cut the nails"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A sponge is used with soap to scrub and clean the skin."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','Rice, yam and garri belong to the food group that gives us ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "air"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sleep"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Carbohydrate foods like rice, yam and garri give the body energy."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','Which of these foods is a good source of protein for building the body?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Beans"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sugar"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Palm oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Salt"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Beans is a protein food that helps build and repair the body."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','Oranges, mango and pawpaw are examples of ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "fruits"}, {"id": "b", "text": "meats"}, {"id": "c", "text": "grains"}, {"id": "d", "text": "oils"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Oranges, mango and pawpaw are fruits rich in vitamins."}',0.3,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','Which of these is a body-building (protein) food?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fish"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Yam"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bread"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rice"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Fish is a protein food that helps build the body."}',0.35,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','Green leafy vegetables like ugu (pumpkin leaves) mainly provide the body with ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "vitamins and minerals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "only fat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only sugar"}, {"id": "d", "text": "only oil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Vegetables such as ugu supply vitamins and minerals that protect the body."}',0.4,'{P4,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
