  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T3','PHE-T3-O2','Regular exercise helps to make which part of the body strong?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The muscles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The chalk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The desk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The football only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Regular exercise builds and strengthens the muscles of the body."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T3','PHE-T3-O2','A person who exercises regularly and is strong and active is said to be what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Physically fit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Always sick"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Very lazy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Weak and tired"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Being physically fit means the body is strong, active and can work without getting tired quickly."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T3','PHE-T3-O2','Which of these is a benefit of taking part in exercise every day?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It helps the heart work well"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It makes you fall sick easily"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It makes the bones weak"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It stops you from growing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Exercise strengthens the heart so that it pumps blood better and keeps you healthy."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T3','PHE-T3-O2','Which of these activities gives the body good exercise?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Skipping with a rope"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Watching television all day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sleeping all afternoon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sitting without moving"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Skipping is an active exercise that keeps the body fit, while sitting or sleeping is not."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T3','PHE-T3-O2','After doing exercise, what should you do to help your body cool down slowly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Do gentle stretching and rest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Run even faster at once"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Jump into cold food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Never rest again"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cooling down with gentle stretching and rest helps the body return to normal safely."}',0.4,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O1','In which athletic event do people run a short, fast race on a track?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sprinting (short-distance race)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Swimming"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Chess"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Drawing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sprinting is a short, fast running race held on a track in athletics."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O1','Long jump and high jump belong to which part of athletics?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Field events"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ball games"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Board games"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Water sports"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jumping and throwing events are called field events in athletics."}',0.4,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O1','In a relay race, what does a runner pass to the next teammate?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A baton"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A football"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A book"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A cup of water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "In a relay race, runners pass a baton from one team member to the next."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O1','Which of these is a throwing field event in athletics?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Shot put"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reading race"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Singing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Marching only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Shot put is a field event in which the athlete throws (puts) a heavy ball as far as possible."}',0.4,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O1','The area with marked lanes where running races take place is called the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The track"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The kitchen"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The classroom"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The market"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Running races are held on the track, which is marked into lanes for the athletes."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O2','How many players make up one football team on the pitch during a match?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Eleven players"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Two players"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Twenty players"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Five players"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A football team has eleven players on the pitch, including the goalkeeper."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O2','Which player in football is the only one allowed to use the hands inside the goal area?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The goalkeeper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The referee"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The striker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The coach"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Only the goalkeeper may handle the ball with the hands within the goal area."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O2','Who blows the whistle and makes sure players obey the rules during a match?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The referee"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The goalkeeper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The captain"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A spectator"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The referee controls the game, blows the whistle and makes sure the rules are followed."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O2','Which piece of equipment is needed to play the game of table tennis?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A bat and a small ball"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A pair of boots only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A skipping rope"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A cooking pot"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Table tennis is played with a bat (paddle) and a small light ball on a table."}',0.4,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T4','PHE-T4-O2','Why is it important to follow the rules and play fairly during a game?','[{"id": "a", "text": "So the game is orderly and enjoyable for everyone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "So one team can cheat easily"}, {"id": "c", "text": "So players can fight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "So the game never ends"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Following the rules and playing fairly keeps the game orderly, safe and enjoyable for all."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O1','What should you do before crossing a busy road?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Look left and right for vehicles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Close your eyes and run across"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Play in the middle of the road"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Lie down on the road"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Looking left and right helps you cross safely when no vehicle is coming."}',0.25,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O1','Which of these is a safety rule when playing on the field?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Do not push or hit other players"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Play with broken bottles"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Run with sharp sticks"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fight when you lose"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Not pushing or hitting others helps prevent injuries during play."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O1','To stay safe at home, sharp knives and hot pots should be kept how?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Away from where small children can reach them"}, {"id": "b", "text": "On the floor for children to play with"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Inside the school bag"}, {"id": "d", "text": "On the child''s bed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Keeping sharp and hot objects out of children''s reach prevents cuts and burns."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O1','Why should you not play with matches, fire or electric sockets?','[{"id": "a", "text": "They can cause burns, fire or electric shock"}, {"id": "b", "text": "They make good toys"}, {"id": "c", "text": "They help you sleep"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They make you grow taller"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Fire and electricity are dangerous and can cause burns, fire outbreaks or shock."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O1','What should you do if you see a broken bottle on the playground?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tell an adult and have it safely removed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Kick it around with your feet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Throw it at a friend"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sit on it"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Reporting the broken bottle to an adult lets it be removed safely before anyone is hurt."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O2','What is the first thing to do to a small cut on the skin?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wash it with clean water and cover it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rub sand into it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Leave it very dirty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Put mud on it"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cleaning a cut with clean water and covering it keeps out germs and helps it heal."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O2','The box that holds bandages, plaster and other items for treating small injuries is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A first aid box"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A lunch box"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A tool box"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A music box"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A first aid box holds items used to give first aid for minor injuries."}',0.3,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O2','Which disease common in Nigeria is spread by the bite of a mosquito?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Malaria"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A broken leg"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Toothache"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hunger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Malaria is spread by the bite of an infected mosquito."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O2','Which of these helps to prevent malaria at home?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sleeping under a treated mosquito net"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keeping stagnant water everywhere"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Leaving windows wide open at night"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Never cleaning the surroundings"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sleeping under a treated mosquito net stops mosquito bites and helps prevent malaria."}',0.35,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','PHE','PHE-T5','PHE-T5-O2','Washing your hands with soap helps to prevent diseases such as which of these?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Diarrhoea and cholera"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A broken arm"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Poor eyesight from birth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tall height"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hand washing removes germs that cause diarrhoea and cholera."}',0.4,'{P4,PHE,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O1','A family made up of a father, a mother and their children only is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "extended family"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nuclear family"}, {"id": "c", "text": "royal family"}, {"id": "d", "text": "polygamous family"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A nuclear family consists of a father, a mother and their children only."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O1','A family that includes grandparents, uncles, aunts and cousins in addition to parents and children is called an','[{"id": "a", "text": "extended family"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nuclear family"}, {"id": "c", "text": "small family"}, {"id": "d", "text": "single family"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An extended family includes relatives such as grandparents, uncles, aunts and cousins."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O1','Who is normally regarded as the head of a typical Nigerian family?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The eldest child"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The mother"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The father"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The house help"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "In a typical Nigerian family the father is regarded as the head of the family."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O1','One important duty of children in the family is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "pay the family''s rent"}, {"id": "b", "text": "obey and respect their parents"}, {"id": "c", "text": "buy the family car"}, {"id": "d", "text": "employ workers for the home"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Children are expected to obey and respect their parents and elders."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O1','The mother''s role of caring for the children and managing the home is best described as','[{"id": "a", "text": "keeping the family together"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ruling the community"}, {"id": "c", "text": "collecting taxes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "trading in the market only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A mother helps keep the family together by caring for the children and managing the home."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O2','One major importance of the family to a child is that it provides','[{"id": "a", "text": "love, food and shelter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "election results"}, {"id": "c", "text": "school certificates"}, {"id": "d", "text": "market prices"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The family provides basic needs such as love, food and shelter for the child."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O2','The family is often called the first place where a child learns because it is where a child first','[{"id": "a", "text": "receives good behaviour and values"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pays school fees"}, {"id": "c", "text": "votes in elections"}, {"id": "d", "text": "gets a driver''s licence"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The family is the first school where a child learns good behaviour and values."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O2','Which of the following is a function of the family?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Making national laws"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Taking care of its sick members"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Printing the country''s money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Building highways"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Caring for its sick and needy members is one of the functions of the family."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O2','When members of a family help and support one another, the family becomes','[{"id": "a", "text": "united and happy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "poor and sad"}, {"id": "c", "text": "divided and weak"}, {"id": "d", "text": "empty and lonely"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cooperation and support make a family united and happy."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T1','SOS-T1-O2','A good way for a child to show love in the family is by','[{"id": "a", "text": "quarrelling with brothers and sisters"}, {"id": "b", "text": "helping with house chores"}, {"id": "c", "text": "refusing to greet elders"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hiding food from others"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Helping with house chores is a good way for a child to show love in the family."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O1','The way of life of a group of people is called their','[{"id": "a", "text": "culture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "money"}, {"id": "c", "text": "map"}, {"id": "d", "text": "weather"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Culture is the total way of life of a group of people."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O1','Which of the following is an example of Nigerian culture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Traditional dances and festivals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The multiplication table"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The rules of football"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The colours of the rainbow"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Traditional dances and festivals are examples of Nigerian culture."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O1','Food, dressing, language and festivals are all parts of a people''s','[{"id": "a", "text": "culture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "salary"}, {"id": "c", "text": "timetable"}, {"id": "d", "text": "temperature"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Food, dressing, language and festivals are all parts of a people''s culture."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O1','The New Yam Festival is a cultural celebration commonly held among the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Igbo people"}, {"id": "b", "text": "people of France"}, {"id": "c", "text": "people of China"}, {"id": "d", "text": "people of America"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The New Yam Festival is widely celebrated among the Igbo people of Nigeria."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O1','Which of these is a Nigerian language?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Spanish"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Yoruba"}, {"id": "c", "text": "German"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Italian"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Yoruba is one of the major languages spoken in Nigeria."}',0.25,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O2','Which of the following is a good cultural value that should be encouraged?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Respect for elders"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Stealing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cheating"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fighting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Respect for elders is a good cultural value worthy of upholding."}',0.25,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O2','Telling the truth at all times is a value known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "honesty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "greed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pride"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Always telling the truth is the value of honesty."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O2','Which of the following is a bad cultural practice that should be discouraged?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hospitality to visitors"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hard work"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cheating in trade"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Respect for parents"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Cheating in trade is a bad practice that should be discouraged."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O2','Welcoming and treating visitors well is a good value called','[{"id": "a", "text": "hospitality"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wickedness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "selfishness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rudeness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Treating visitors kindly and warmly is called hospitality."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T2','SOS-T2-O2','A pupil who works hard and finishes his duties is showing the value of','[{"id": "a", "text": "diligence"}, {"id": "b", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dishonesty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "carelessness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Working hard and completing duties shows diligence."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O1','A group of families living together in the same area is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "community"}, {"id": "b", "text": "continent"}, {"id": "c", "text": "planet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "factory"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A community is a group of families living together in the same area."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O1','Which of the following is a social group found in the school?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The Press Club"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The national army"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The state government"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The central bank"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Press Club is an example of a social group within the school."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O1','Age grades, town unions and cooperative societies are examples of','[{"id": "a", "text": "social groups"}, {"id": "b", "text": "farm tools"}, {"id": "c", "text": "school subjects"}, {"id": "d", "text": "types of food"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Age grades, town unions and cooperative societies are all social groups."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O1','One main reason people form social groups is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "help one another and solve common problems"}, {"id": "b", "text": "quarrel with one another"}, {"id": "c", "text": "waste their time"}, {"id": "d", "text": "avoid meeting people"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "People form social groups to help one another and solve common problems."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O1','A group formed by people who worship together is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "religious group"}, {"id": "b", "text": "football club"}, {"id": "c", "text": "farming group"}, {"id": "d", "text": "market group"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "People who worship together belong to a religious group."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O2','When people work together to achieve a common goal, it is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "cooperation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "competition"}, {"id": "c", "text": "confusion"}, {"id": "d", "text": "quarrel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Working together for a common goal is called cooperation."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O2','Which of the following helps people to live peacefully in a community?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tolerance and understanding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fighting and quarrelling"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cheating neighbours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stealing from others"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tolerance and understanding help people to live peacefully together."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O2','Community members joining hands to clear a blocked road is an example of','[{"id": "a", "text": "communal cooperation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "selfishness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stealing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "laziness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "People working together to clear a road shows communal cooperation."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O2','A good neighbour is one who','[{"id": "a", "text": "helps others in times of need"}, {"id": "b", "text": "makes noise at night"}, {"id": "c", "text": "refuses to greet people"}, {"id": "d", "text": "damages other people''s property"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A good neighbour helps others in times of need."}',0.25,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T3','SOS-T3-O2','Peace in a community is best kept when people','[{"id": "a", "text": "settle their differences without violence"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fight over small matters"}, {"id": "c", "text": "refuse to obey rules"}, {"id": "d", "text": "insult one another"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Settling differences peacefully, without violence, keeps peace in a community."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','Which of the following is a natural feature of the environment?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A river"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A bridge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A road"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A house"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A river is a natural feature because it is not made by people."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','Which of the following is a man-made feature?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A building"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A mountain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A forest"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The sun"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A building is a man-made feature because it is constructed by people."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','The gifts of nature such as land, water, air and minerals are called','[{"id": "a", "text": "natural resources"}, {"id": "b", "text": "school fees"}, {"id": "c", "text": "man-made goods"}, {"id": "d", "text": "factory machines"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Land, water, air and minerals are natural resources given by nature."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','Which of the following natural resources is Nigeria well known for exporting?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Crude oil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ice blocks"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Snow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Plastic bags"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Nigeria is well known for its crude oil, an important natural resource."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O1','Hills, valleys and rivers together make up the ______ of a place.','[{"id": "a", "text": "physical features"}, {"id": "b", "text": "school subjects"}, {"id": "c", "text": "market goods"}, {"id": "d", "text": "family members"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hills, valleys and rivers are the physical (natural) features of a place."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','A good way to keep our environment clean is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "dispose of refuse properly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "throw rubbish into rivers"}, {"id": "c", "text": "burn tyres near houses"}, {"id": "d", "text": "leave dirty water everywhere"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Disposing of refuse properly helps keep the environment clean."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','Planting trees helps the environment because trees','[{"id": "a", "text": "give us fresh air and shade"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cause more pollution"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make the ground dirty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "block clean water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Trees provide fresh air and shade, which helps the environment."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','Blocked drainages in a community can lead to','[{"id": "a", "text": "flooding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "clean streets"}, {"id": "c", "text": "good roads"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fresh air"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "When drainages are blocked, water cannot flow away and flooding can occur."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','Which of the following actions pollutes the environment?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pouring waste into streams"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sweeping the compound"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Planting flowers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clearing gutters"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Pouring waste into streams pollutes the water and the environment."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T4','SOS-T4-O2','Community sanitation exercises are organised mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "keep the surroundings clean and healthy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase dirt in the area"}, {"id": "c", "text": "block all the roads"}, {"id": "d", "text": "chase away visitors"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sanitation exercises are organised to keep surroundings clean and healthy."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','A person who belongs to a country and enjoys its rights is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "citizen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "visitor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stranger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "tourist"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A citizen is a person who belongs to a country and enjoys its rights."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','Which of the following is a duty of a good citizen?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Obeying the laws of the land"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Refusing to pay taxes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Destroying public property"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Disturbing the peace"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Obeying the laws of the land is a duty of a good citizen."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','Every Nigerian child has a right to','[{"id": "a", "text": "education"}, {"id": "b", "text": "break the law"}, {"id": "c", "text": "avoid all rules"}, {"id": "d", "text": "damage schools"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Every Nigerian child has a right to education."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','Paying tax to the government is an example of a citizen''s','[{"id": "a", "text": "duty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "holiday"}, {"id": "c", "text": "game"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reward"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Paying tax is one of the duties of a citizen."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O1','A good citizen protects public property such as schools and hospitals by','[{"id": "a", "text": "using them carefully and not damaging them"}, {"id": "b", "text": "writing on the walls"}, {"id": "c", "text": "breaking the windows"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stealing the equipment"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A good citizen uses public property carefully and avoids damaging it."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','The two main colours of the Nigerian national flag are','[{"id": "a", "text": "green and white"}, {"id": "b", "text": "red and blue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "yellow and black"}, {"id": "d", "text": "orange and purple"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Nigerian national flag is green, white and green."}',0.25,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','The white colour in the Nigerian flag stands for','[{"id": "a", "text": "peace and unity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "war"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hunger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "danger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The white in the Nigerian flag stands for peace and unity."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','The green colour in the Nigerian flag represents','[{"id": "a", "text": "agriculture and rich farmland"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the ocean"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gold and money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the night sky"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The green in the flag represents agriculture and Nigeria''s rich farmland."}',0.35,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','Which of the following is a national symbol of Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The Coat of Arms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A football jersey"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A market stall"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A school bag"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Coat of Arms is one of Nigeria''s national symbols."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P4','SOS','SOS-T5','SOS-T5-O2','We show respect for the national anthem by','[{"id": "a", "text": "standing at attention while it is sung"}, {"id": "b", "text": "talking loudly during it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sitting and playing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "walking away"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "We show respect for the national anthem by standing at attention while it is sung."}',0.3,'{P4,SOS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','Which farm tool is used mainly for digging and turning the soil during land preparation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hoe"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rake"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wheelbarrow"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The hoe is used for digging, weeding and turning the soil."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','A farmer wants to clear tall grasses and bushes on his farmland. Which tool is most suitable?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Watering can"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hand trowel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hand fork"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The cutlass is used for clearing bushes and cutting grasses."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','Which tool is best used for transplanting young seedlings from the nursery to the field?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rake"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hand trowel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Axe"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The hand trowel is used for lifting and transplanting seedlings."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','What is the main use of a watering can on the farm?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To cut down trees"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To apply water to plants"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To carry loads"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To make ridges"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A watering can is used to water plants, especially seedlings in the nursery."}',0.25,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O1','Which of these tools is used for gathering dry leaves and levelling the soil surface?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rake"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sickle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Spade"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cutlass"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The rake is used to gather leaves and level the soil surface."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','Why should farm tools be cleaned after use?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To make them heavier"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To prevent rusting and damage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To make them blunt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To change their colour"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cleaning tools after use prevents rust and keeps them in good condition."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','What should a farmer apply to the metal parts of tools to prevent rusting during storage?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Oil or grease"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Salt"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Applying oil or grease to metal parts protects them from rust."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','Cutting tools like the cutlass and hoe should be sharpened regularly so that they can:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Become rusty quickly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Work efficiently and cut easily"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Break into pieces"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Become heavier"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sharp tools cut easily and make farm work faster and more efficient."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','Where should farm tools be kept after use?','[{"id": "a", "text": "In the rain"}, {"id": "b", "text": "In a dry store or tool shed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Inside a river"}, {"id": "d", "text": "On wet ground"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Tools should be stored in a dry place to prevent rust and damage."}',0.25,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T1','AGR-T1-O2','A tool with a loose wooden handle should be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Thrown away immediately"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Used as it is"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Repaired by fixing the handle firmly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Soaked in water"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A loose handle should be repaired and fixed firmly to make the tool safe to use."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','Which of these is the first stage in crop production?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Harvesting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Land clearing and preparation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Weeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Storage"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Land clearing and preparation is the first stage before planting."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','The removal of unwanted plants growing among crops is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Weeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Planting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Harvesting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mulching"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weeding is the removal of weeds that compete with crops for nutrients."}',0.25,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','Adding manure or fertiliser to the soil to make crops grow well is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Harvesting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Manuring"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Clearing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Threshing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Manuring is adding manure or fertiliser to supply nutrients to crops."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','Covering the soil surface with dry leaves or grasses to conserve moisture is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mulching"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Weeding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pruning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Harvesting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Mulching covers the soil to conserve moisture and control weeds."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O1','The gathering of matured crops from the farm is known as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Planting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Harvesting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nursing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clearing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Harvesting is the collection of matured crops from the farm."}',0.25,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','Crops such as maize, rice and guinea corn that provide starch are grouped as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cereal crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Leguminous crops"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fruit crops"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fibre crops"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Maize, rice and guinea corn are cereal (grain) crops rich in starch."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','Which of these is a leguminous crop that adds nitrogen to the soil?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cowpea"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Maize"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cassava"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cowpea (beans) is a legume that fixes nitrogen into the soil."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','Cassava and yam are examples of which group of crops?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fruit crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cereal crops"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Root and tuber crops"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Vegetable crops"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Cassava and yam store food in roots and tubers underground."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','A crop that completes its life cycle within one growing season is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "An annual crop"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A perennial crop"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A biennial crop"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A permanent crop"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Annual crops like maize complete their life cycle in one season."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T2','AGR-T2-O2','Which of these is a perennial crop that lives for many years?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Maize"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tomato"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Oil palm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rice"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Oil palm is a perennial crop that grows and yields for many years."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Cattle, goats and sheep that feed mainly on grasses are grouped as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Poultry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ruminants"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fish"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Reptiles"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cattle, goats and sheep are ruminants that chew the cud."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Which farm animal is kept mainly for the production of eggs?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Goat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pig"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The hen (poultry) is kept mainly for eggs and meat."}',0.25,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','The main product obtained from a dairy cow is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Egg"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Milk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wool"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Honey"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dairy cattle are reared mainly for milk production."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Which of these animals is reared mainly for its meat, known as pork?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pig"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sheep"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rabbit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Duck"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Pigs are reared mainly for pork (their meat)."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O1','Honey is a farm product obtained from:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bees"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Goats"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fowls"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fish"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Honey is produced by bees kept in an apiary (bee-keeping)."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','Which of these is most important for keeping farm animals healthy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Providing clean water and good feed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Leaving them without food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keeping them in dirty pens"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Denying them water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clean water and good feed keep farm animals healthy and productive."}',0.25,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','The building where poultry birds are kept is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Kennel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Poultry house"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Barn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Silo"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Poultry birds are housed in a poultry house or pen."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','Giving drugs or injections to protect animals against diseases is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Vaccination"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Weeding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grazing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Milking"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Vaccination protects animals against common diseases."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','Why should the animal house be kept clean at all times?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To attract more flies"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To prevent diseases and infections"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To make animals sick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To waste feed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A clean animal house prevents the spread of diseases and pests."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T3','AGR-T3-O2','Feeds that supply mainly protein for the growth of young animals include:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Groundnut cake and soya beans"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pure water only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sand and stones"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Dry firewood"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Groundnut cake and soya beans are protein-rich feeds for growth."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','Which of these is a component of the soil?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mineral particles, water, air and humus"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Only plastic"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only stones"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Only metal"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Soil is made up of mineral particles, water, air, humus and living organisms."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','The dark part of the soil formed from decayed plants and animals is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sand"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Humus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Clay"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Gravel"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Humus is the dark, fertile material formed from decayed organic matter."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','Which type of soil holds water for a long time and is sticky when wet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sandy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clay soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Gravel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ash"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clay soil holds water and is sticky when wet."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','Why is soil important to plants?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It gives plants shade only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It anchors plants and supplies nutrients and water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It only makes the ground dirty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It has no use to plants"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Soil holds plant roots firmly and supplies nutrients and water."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O1','Which soil is loose, drains water quickly and is best for growing groundnut?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Clay soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sandy soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Loamy soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rocky soil"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sandy soil drains quickly and suits crops like groundnut."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','Water is important to crops because it helps them to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make food and stay fresh"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Dry up quickly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Die faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stop growing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Water helps crops make food through photosynthesis and stay healthy."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','The gas in the air that green plants use to make their food is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Oxygen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Carbon dioxide"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nitrogen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hydrogen"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Green plants use carbon dioxide from the air during photosynthesis."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','The supply of water to crops through channels or pipes during the dry season is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Drainage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Irrigation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Weeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mulching"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Irrigation is supplying water to crops, especially in the dry season."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','Farm animals need air mainly for:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Breathing (respiration)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Swimming"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Flying"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sleeping"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Animals need oxygen from the air for breathing (respiration)."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T4','AGR-T4-O2','The removal of excess water from waterlogged farmland is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Irrigation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Drainage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Planting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Harvesting"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Drainage removes excess water from waterlogged soil."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','Which of these is a common pest that destroys stored grains like maize?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Weevil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Earthworm"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bee"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Butterfly"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weevils attack and destroy stored grains such as maize and beans."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','Rats and grasscutters are pests because they:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Improve the soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Eat and destroy crops"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Water the plants"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Add nutrients to crops"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rodents like rats and grasscutters feed on and destroy crops."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','Birds such as weaver birds are serious pests of which crop on Nigerian farms?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rice"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cassava"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Yam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cocoyam"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weaver birds feed on ripening grains like rice, causing heavy losses."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','Insect pests like grasshoppers damage crops mainly by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watering the leaves"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Eating the leaves and stems"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Adding manure"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pollinating flowers"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Grasshoppers feed on leaves and stems, reducing crop yield."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O1','A pest is best described as any:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Animal or insect that damages crops or animals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tool used on the farm"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Type of fertiliser"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Helpful earthworm"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A pest is any organism that damages crops, animals or farm produce."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','Chemicals used to kill insect pests on the farm are called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Insecticides"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fertilisers"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Manures"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Vitamins"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Insecticides are chemicals used to control and kill insect pests."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','Which of these is a simple way to control birds on a maize farm?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Using a scarecrow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Adding more water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Planting more weeds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leaving the farm dirty"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A scarecrow frightens birds away from the crops."}',0.3,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','Storing grains in a clean, dry place helps to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Attract more weevils"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reduce pest damage during storage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Make the grains rot"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase moisture"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clean, dry storage protects grains from pests and spoilage."}',0.35,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','Diseases in crops and animals are often caused by tiny organisms called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Germs (micro-organisms)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tractors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ridges"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fertilisers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Germs or micro-organisms such as bacteria and fungi cause many diseases."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','AGR','AGR-T5','AGR-T5-O2','One good farming practice that helps to reduce pests and diseases is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Crop rotation and keeping the farm clean"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Never removing weeds"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Planting the same crop forever"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leaving dead animals on the farm"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Crop rotation and farm sanitation reduce the build-up of pests and diseases."}',0.4,'{P5,AGR,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','Which of these is a group of the three primary colours?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Red, blue and yellow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Green, orange and purple"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Black, white and grey"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pink, brown and gold"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Red, blue and yellow are the primary colours from which other colours are made."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','When you mix blue and yellow paint together, which colour do you get?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Purple"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Green"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Orange"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Brown"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Blue mixed with yellow produces the secondary colour green."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','Which of the following is a secondary colour?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yellow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Orange"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Red"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Orange is a secondary colour made by mixing red and yellow."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','Mixing red and blue paint together gives which colour?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Green"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Orange"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Purple"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Yellow"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Red combined with blue produces the secondary colour purple."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O1','Colours such as green, orange and purple are called what type of colours?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Primary colours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Secondary colours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Neutral colours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Warm colours"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Secondary colours are formed by mixing two primary colours."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','Which tool is best for making a light drawing that can easily be rubbed off?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pencil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ink pen"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Crayon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Candle"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A pencil makes light marks that can be erased with a rubber."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','Which object is used to erase pencil marks when drawing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Ruler"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Eraser"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Brush"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sharpener"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An eraser (rubber) is used to remove pencil marks from paper."}',0.25,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','A dot that moves along a surface to join two points forms what element of art?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A shape"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A line"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A texture"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A line is formed when a point moves across a surface."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','Which of these is used to apply paint onto paper during painting?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Brush"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Scissors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Needle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hammer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A brush is the tool used to spread paint on a surface."}',0.25,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T1','CCA-T1-O2','A round shape like a ball or the sun is best described as what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A square"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A triangle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A circle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A rectangle"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A round shape with no corners is called a circle."}',0.25,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Which local craft is made by weaving palm fronds or raffia into containers?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Basket making"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pottery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Carving"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Painting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Basket making uses woven palm fronds, cane or raffia."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Clay is the main material used to make which of these crafts?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pots"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mats"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cloth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Beads"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clay is moulded and fired to make pots in pottery."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Adire, a popular Yoruba craft, is made by dyeing what material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wood"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cloth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Metal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stone"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Adire is a resist-dyed cloth made mostly by the Yoruba people."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Which material is used by a carver to make traditional wooden stools and masks?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wood"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clay"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Raffia"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cotton"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Carvers use wood to make stools, masks and figures."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O1','Sleeping mats in many Nigerian villages are commonly woven from what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Metal wires"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reeds or raffia"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Glass"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Plastic pipes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Mats are traditionally woven from reeds, raffia or palm fronds."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','Before a clay pot can be shaped, the clay must first be made ready by doing what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Kneading and mixing it with water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Burning it in fire"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Painting it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cutting it with scissors"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clay is kneaded and mixed with water to make it soft and workable."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','After a clay pot is shaped, it is made strong and hard by doing what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Soaking it in water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Firing (baking) it with heat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Leaving it in the fridge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wrapping it in cloth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Firing the pot with heat makes it hard and durable."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','In making adire cloth, patterns are created by tying parts of the cloth before doing what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Dyeing it in colour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sewing buttons on it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ironing it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Folding it into a bag"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tied areas resist the dye, forming patterns when the cloth is dyed."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','What is the first thing a basket weaver needs before starting to weave a basket?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Weaving materials like cane or raffia"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A tin of paint"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A bag of clay"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A block of wood"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The weaver first gathers cane, raffia or palm fronds to weave with."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T2','CCA-T2-O2','Which tool does a carver mainly use to cut and shape wood into a figure?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A chisel and mallet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A paint brush"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A sewing needle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A cooking pot"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Carvers use a chisel struck with a mallet to shape wood."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','The ''gangan'' or talking drum produces sound when it is what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Beaten with a stick"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blown with the mouth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Plucked with the fingers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Shaken from side to side"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The talking drum is a percussion instrument beaten with a curved stick."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','The ''sekere'' (shekere) makes sound when it is what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Blown"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Shaken"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bowed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Struck with a hammer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The sekere is a gourd covered with beads that rattle when shaken."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','Which of these instruments is played by blowing air into it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Flute"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Drum"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Gong"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Maracas"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A flute is a wind instrument that sounds when air is blown into it."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','Instruments that are beaten or struck to make sound are called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wind instruments"}, {"id": "b", "text": "String instruments"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Percussion instruments"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Electric instruments"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Percussion instruments produce sound when struck or beaten."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O1','The ''goje'', a traditional northern Nigerian instrument, produces sound when its string is what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bowed or rubbed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blown"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shaken"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Beaten with a stick"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The goje is a stringed instrument played by rubbing a bow across its string."}',0.45,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','The regular pattern of sound and silence in music is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rhythm"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shape"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Texture"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Rhythm is the pattern of sounds and silences in music."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','The steady pulse you clap along to in a song is called the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Beat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Line"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Verse"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Title"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The beat is the steady pulse felt throughout a piece of music."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','The words of a song are known as the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Lyrics"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Melody"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Drum"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stage"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The lyrics are the words that are sung in a song."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','When one person sings a line and others answer, the singing style is called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Call and response"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Solo only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Silent reading"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Whispering"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Call and response is a leader-and-chorus style common in African songs."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T3','CCA-T3-O2','How fast or slow a song is sung or played is known as the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tempo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Line"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Weight"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tempo describes the speed at which music is performed."}',0.45,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','The ''Atilogwu'' is an energetic traditional dance of which Nigerian group?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Igbo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hausa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Efik"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tiv"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Atilogwu is a lively acrobatic dance of the Igbo people."}',0.45,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','A dance performed to celebrate the harvesting of crops is called a what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "War dance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Harvest dance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Funeral dance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Coronation dance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A harvest dance celebrates a successful gathering of crops."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','A play acted on stage before an audience is an example of what art form?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Drama"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pottery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Weaving"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Painting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Drama is a story acted out by performers before an audience."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','A performer who wears a costume and pretends to be another character in a play is called a what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Actor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Farmer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Driver"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Trader"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An actor plays the part of a character in a drama."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O1','A masquerade performance, common at Nigerian festivals, usually combines dance with what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Masks and costumes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cooking food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Selling goods"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Reading books"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Masquerades wear masks and colourful costumes while dancing."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','The person who guides the actors and controls how a play is performed is the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Director"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Audience"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Gatekeeper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cook"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The director guides the actors and organises the performance."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','The people who come to watch a drama performance are called the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Audience"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Actors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Directors"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Dancers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The audience is the group of people who watch a performance."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','The special clothes worn by actors to suit their characters are called what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Costumes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tickets"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Scripts"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Chairs"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Costumes are the dress worn by actors to fit their roles."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','The written words and instructions that actors follow in a play are found in the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Script"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Basket"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Drum"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Curtain"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A script contains the dialogue and directions for a play."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T4','CCA-T4-O2','The raised platform where actors perform a play is called the what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Market"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Kitchen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Garden"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The stage is the area where actors perform before an audience."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','The Argungu Fishing Festival is famous for the activity of what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fishing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wrestling only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Farming"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Boat building"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Argungu festival in Kebbi State is well known for its fishing competition."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','The New Yam Festival is celebrated mainly to do what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Give thanks for a good harvest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mark the rainy season"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Open a new market"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Start a football match"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The New Yam Festival celebrates and gives thanks for the yam harvest."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','The Durbar festival, common in northern Nigeria, is well known for its display of what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Decorated horses and riders"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fishing nets"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Clay pots"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Swimming races"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Durbar features a colourful parade of horse riders and horses."}',0.4,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','The Osun-Osogbo festival is held in honour of a river goddess beside which river?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The Osun River"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The Niger River"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The Benue River"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The Kaduna River"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Osun-Osogbo festival honours the goddess of the Osun River."}',0.45,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O1','Festivals help to do which of the following in a community?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Preserve and celebrate culture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Destroy tradition"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stop people from meeting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "End all farming"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Festivals help to keep and celebrate a people''s culture and traditions."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','The ''agbada'' is a traditional flowing gown worn mostly by which group?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Yoruba men"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Only children"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Foreign tourists"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Nobody today"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The agbada is a large flowing robe worn traditionally by Yoruba men."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','Which of these is a popular traditional Nigerian food made from cassava?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Garri (eba)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pizza"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Burger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Spaghetti"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Garri, used to make eba, is processed from cassava tubers."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','The green colour on the Nigerian national flag stands for what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Agriculture and rich farmland"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The ocean"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Gold and money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The sky"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The green stripes represent Nigeria''s agriculture and natural wealth."}',0.35,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','The white part of the Nigerian flag stands for what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Peace and unity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "War"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hunger"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Darkness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The white centre of the flag represents peace and unity."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CCA','CCA-T5','CCA-T5-O2','Respecting the culture and traditions of other Nigerian ethnic groups helps to promote what?','[{"id": "a", "text": "National unity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fighting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hatred"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Confusion"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Respecting other cultures builds peace and national unity."}',0.3,'{P5,CCA,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','National values are the accepted standards of behaviour that a country expects from all its citizens. Which of the following is a national value?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cheating in examinations"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Honesty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stealing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fighting"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Honesty is a national value that guides good behaviour among citizens."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','A pupil who tells the truth at all times and never cheats is showing which national value?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Honesty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Laziness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Greed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pride"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Always telling the truth and refusing to cheat are signs of honesty."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','When members of a class work together to keep their classroom clean, they are practising the value of ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "cooperation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "selfishness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "quarrelling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "disobedience"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Working together for a common goal is called cooperation."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','A soldier who obeys orders and keeps to the rules of the army is showing the value of ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "discipline"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lateness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rudeness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "carelessness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Obeying rules and orders is a sign of discipline."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O1','Which of these best explains the meaning of national values?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rules only for children in school"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Standards of good behaviour expected of all citizens of a country"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Songs sung at football matches"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Money paid to the government"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "National values are the good standards of behaviour a country expects from its citizens."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','Ada found a wallet full of money on her way to school and returned it to the owner. Which national value did Ada show?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Honesty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wickedness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Jealousy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Greed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Returning found property to its owner shows honesty."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','Why is cooperation important in a community?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It helps people finish difficult tasks faster by working together"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It makes people fight one another"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It encourages laziness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It makes work harder for everyone"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cooperation lets people combine their efforts and finish tasks more easily."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','A country where most citizens are honest and hardworking will most likely ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "develop and progress"}, {"id": "b", "text": "become poorer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "have more crime"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stop growing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Honest and hardworking citizens help a nation to develop and progress."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','Musa always arrives at school before the bell rings and finishes his work on time. Which value is he practising?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Punctuality"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Truancy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dishonesty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rudeness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Coming early and finishing work on time shows punctuality."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T1','CIV-T1-O2','Which of the following actions shows a lack of good national values?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Helping an old woman cross the road"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Telling lies to escape punishment"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keeping your environment clean"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Respecting your teachers"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Telling lies is dishonesty, which is against good national values."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','A citizen is a person who ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "belongs to a country and enjoys its rights and privileges"}, {"id": "b", "text": "is only visiting a country for a short time"}, {"id": "c", "text": "has no country at all"}, {"id": "d", "text": "works only in a market"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A citizen is a full member of a country who enjoys its rights and privileges."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','A child born in Nigeria to Nigerian parents becomes a citizen by ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "birth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "trading"}, {"id": "c", "text": "farming"}, {"id": "d", "text": "visiting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Being born in the country to citizen parents makes one a citizen by birth."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','A foreigner who marries a Nigerian and later becomes a Nigerian citizen has become a citizen by ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "registration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stealing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "singing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dancing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Citizenship gained through marriage to a citizen is citizenship by registration."}',0.45,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','Which of these people is NOT a citizen of Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A tourist visiting Nigeria for two weeks"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A child born in Lagos to Nigerian parents"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A man born in Kano whose parents are Nigerians"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A woman who was granted Nigerian citizenship"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A tourist only visits for a short time and is not a citizen."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O1','The three main ways of becoming a Nigerian citizen are by birth, registration and ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "naturalisation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shopping"}, {"id": "c", "text": "swimming"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cooking"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The three ways are by birth, registration and naturalisation."}',0.45,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','Which of the following is a duty of a good citizen?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Paying tax as at when due"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Refusing to obey the law"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Destroying public property"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Avoiding all work"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Paying tax when it is due is an important duty of every citizen."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','The right to attend school and learn is known as the right to ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "education"}, {"id": "b", "text": "vote"}, {"id": "c", "text": "travel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "trade"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Being able to go to school is the right to education."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','Obeying the laws of the country is a ______ of every citizen.','[{"id": "a", "text": "duty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "game"}, {"id": "c", "text": "reward"}, {"id": "d", "text": "holiday"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Obeying the law is a duty every citizen must perform."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','Which of the following is a right enjoyed by Nigerian citizens?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Right to life"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Right to steal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Right to cheat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Right to fight others"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The right to life is a fundamental right of every citizen."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T2','CIV-T2-O2','When a citizen refuses to perform his duties, the society will most likely ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "suffer and not develop well"}, {"id": "b", "text": "become very rich"}, {"id": "c", "text": "grow faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "become more peaceful"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "If citizens neglect their duties, the society suffers and does not develop well."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','Democracy is a system of government in which ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "the people choose their leaders through voting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "only one family rules forever"}, {"id": "c", "text": "soldiers seize power by force"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a king rules without the people"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "In a democracy the people choose their leaders through voting."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','The famous saying that democracy is ''government of the people, by the people and for the people'' was made by ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "Abraham Lincoln"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Nelson Mandela"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nnamdi Azikiwe"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Kwame Nkrumah"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Abraham Lincoln gave the famous definition of democracy."}',0.45,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','Which of these is a feature of democracy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Free and fair elections"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ruling by force"}, {"id": "c", "text": "No respect for the people"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Only one candidate allowed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Free and fair elections are an important feature of democracy."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','In a democracy, the leaders rule based on the wishes of ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "the people"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the soldiers alone"}, {"id": "c", "text": "foreigners"}, {"id": "d", "text": "one rich man"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Democratic leaders rule according to the wishes of the people."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O1','Which type of government is the OPPOSITE of democracy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Military rule by force"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Government chosen by the people"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Government that holds free elections"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Government that respects people''s rights"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Military rule by force is the opposite of democratic government."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','In Nigeria, the body that organises and conducts elections is ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "INEC"}, {"id": "b", "text": "NEPA"}, {"id": "c", "text": "NNPC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "WAEC"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "INEC (Independent National Electoral Commission) conducts elections in Nigeria."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','Before a citizen can vote in Nigeria, he or she must first ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "register and collect a voter''s card"}, {"id": "b", "text": "buy a car"}, {"id": "c", "text": "travel abroad"}, {"id": "d", "text": "join the army"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A citizen must register and get a voter''s card before voting."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','In Nigeria, a person must be at least ______ years old to vote.','[{"id": "a", "text": "18"}, {"id": "b", "text": "10"}, {"id": "c", "text": "12"}, {"id": "d", "text": "60"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The voting age in Nigeria is 18 years."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','Why is voting important in a democracy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It allows citizens to choose their own leaders"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It helps people avoid school"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It is a way to make money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It is only for the rich"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Voting lets citizens choose the leaders they want."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T3','CIV-T3-O2','One good thing about democracy is that it ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "respects the rights and freedom of the people"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stops people from talking"}, {"id": "c", "text": "allows only soldiers to rule"}, {"id": "d", "text": "takes away people''s freedom"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Democracy protects and respects the rights and freedom of the people."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','Human rights are the basic things that every person is entitled to simply because ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "they are human beings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "they are rich"}, {"id": "c", "text": "they own a car"}, {"id": "d", "text": "they are adults"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Human rights belong to every person because they are human beings."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','Which of the following is a right of the child?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The right to education"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The right to do dangerous work"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The right to be beaten"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The right to be starved"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Every child has the right to education."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','The right to good food, medicine and care is the child''s right to ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "health"}, {"id": "b", "text": "voting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "trading"}, {"id": "d", "text": "driving"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Good food, medicine and care are part of the child''s right to health."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','Which of these is a basic human right?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The right to life"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The right to steal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The right to cheat others"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The right to destroy property"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The right to life is one of the most basic human rights."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O1','A child who is given a name and cared for by a family is enjoying the right to ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "a name and family care"}, {"id": "b", "text": "own a company"}, {"id": "c", "text": "carry a gun"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rule the country"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Every child has a right to a name and to be cared for by a family."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','The law in Nigeria that protects the rights of children is called the ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "Child''s Rights Act"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Traffic Law"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Market Law"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Football Law"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Child''s Rights Act protects the rights of children in Nigeria."}',0.45,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','Making a child of school age work all day instead of going to school is called ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "child labour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "child care"}, {"id": "c", "text": "child education"}, {"id": "d", "text": "child play"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Forcing a child to work instead of learning is child labour, which abuses their rights."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','Along with rights, every child also has ______ to perform.','[{"id": "a", "text": "duties"}, {"id": "b", "text": "holidays"}, {"id": "c", "text": "prizes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "salaries"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Rights go together with duties that every child must perform."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','Which of the following is a duty of a child at home?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Helping with house chores"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Refusing to obey parents"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fighting with brothers and sisters"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Destroying household property"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Helping with house chores is a good duty of a child at home."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T4','CIV-T4-O2','If a child''s rights are denied, the child can be helped by ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "reporting to an adult or the authorities"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keeping quiet forever"}, {"id": "c", "text": "running away from home"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fighting everyone"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A child whose rights are denied should report to a trusted adult or the authorities."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','The colours of the Nigerian national flag are ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "green, white and green"}, {"id": "b", "text": "red, white and blue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "black and white"}, {"id": "d", "text": "yellow and green"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Nigerian flag has three vertical stripes of green, white and green."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','The white colour in the Nigerian flag stands for ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "peace and unity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "war"}, {"id": "c", "text": "money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hunger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The white stripe on the flag stands for peace and unity."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','The green colour in the Nigerian flag stands for ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "agriculture and the rich land"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the sea"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the sky"}, {"id": "d", "text": "gold"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The green stripes stand for Nigeria''s agriculture and rich, fertile land."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','Which of the following is a national symbol of Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The Coat of Arms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A market basket"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A football boot"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A cooking pot"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Coat of Arms is one of Nigeria''s national symbols."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O1','The song that citizens sing to show love and loyalty to their country is the ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "national anthem"}, {"id": "b", "text": "birthday song"}, {"id": "c", "text": "market song"}, {"id": "d", "text": "play song"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The national anthem is sung to show love and loyalty to the country."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','When the national anthem is being sung, a good citizen should ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "stand at attention"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keep playing football"}, {"id": "c", "text": "eat and talk loudly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lie down and sleep"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Standing at attention shows respect while the national anthem is sung."}',0.3,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','Loving and being ready to serve one''s country is called ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "patriotism"}, {"id": "b", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "selfishness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "greed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Love for one''s country and willingness to serve it is called patriotism."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','Which of these actions shows respect for the national flag?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Not allowing it to touch the ground"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Using it to clean the floor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tearing it into pieces"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Throwing it in the dustbin"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Keeping the flag from touching the ground shows respect for it."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','A patriotic pupil who wants to help her country should ______.','[{"id": "a", "text": "study hard and obey the rules"}, {"id": "b", "text": "refuse to go to school"}, {"id": "c", "text": "destroy public property"}, {"id": "d", "text": "disobey her teachers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Studying hard and obeying rules is a good way for a pupil to serve the country."}',0.35,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CIV','CIV-T5','CIV-T5-O2','Which of the following is NOT a way of showing patriotism?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Vandalising public pipes and cables"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Paying taxes when due"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keeping the environment clean"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Obeying the laws of the land"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Vandalising public property is unpatriotic; it harms the nation."}',0.4,'{P5,CIV,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','According to the book of Genesis, how many days did God take to complete the work of creation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Five days"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Six days"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Seven days"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ten days"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "God created everything in six days and rested on the seventh."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','On the first day of creation, what did God make?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The sun and the moon"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Light"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fish and birds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Human beings"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "God said, ''Let there be light,'' and there was light on the first day."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','What did God create on the day that He rested from all His work?','[{"id": "a", "text": "He created the animals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "He created the stars"}, {"id": "c", "text": "He created nothing; He rested"}, {"id": "d", "text": "He created the rivers"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "On the seventh day God rested and made it holy, creating nothing new."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','According to Genesis, the first man that God created was named:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Noah"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Abraham"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Adam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Moses"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "God formed the first man, Adam, from the dust of the ground."}',0.25,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O1','From what did God form the first woman, Eve?','[{"id": "a", "text": "From the dust of the ground"}, {"id": "b", "text": "From a rib taken from the man"}, {"id": "c", "text": "From the water of a river"}, {"id": "d", "text": "From the leaves of a tree"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "God made the woman from a rib He took from the man''s side."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','God told the first people to ''have dominion'' over the earth. This means they were to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Destroy all the animals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rule over and care for creation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sell the trees for money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leave the earth empty"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Having dominion means to rule wisely and take care of what God made."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','Which of these actions best shows that a Christian pupil is caring for God''s creation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutting down trees for fun"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Throwing rubbish into the river"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Watering plants and keeping the environment clean"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Killing birds with a catapult"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Keeping the environment clean and tending plants shows care for creation."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','When God finished making the world, He looked at everything He had made and saw that it was:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Very good"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Not useful"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Broken"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Empty"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God saw that all He had made was very good."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','Caring for God''s creation teaches Christians to be good ______ of what God has given them.','[{"id": "a", "text": "enemies"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stewards"}, {"id": "c", "text": "strangers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "traders"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A steward carefully manages and protects what has been entrusted to them."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T1','CRS-T1-O2','A Christian who wastes water and litters the school compound is failing to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "care for God''s creation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "read the Bible"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sing in the choir"}, {"id": "d", "text": "attend church"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Wasting resources and littering shows a failure to care for creation."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','What was the original name of Abraham before God changed it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Abram"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Isaac"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Jacob"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Lot"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God changed Abram''s name to Abraham as part of His covenant."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','From which city did God call Abraham to leave and go to a land He would show him?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Jerusalem"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ur of the Chaldeans"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Egypt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Babylon"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Abraham was called out of Ur of the Chaldeans to a new land."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','What was the name of Abraham''s wife?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rebecca"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rachel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sarah"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leah"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Abraham''s wife was Sarah, formerly called Sarai."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','God promised Abraham that his descendants would be as many as the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "stars in the sky"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fishes in the pond"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hills of the land"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cities of Egypt"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God promised Abraham descendants as numerous as the stars of heaven."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O1','The son of promise that God gave to Abraham and Sarah in their old age was named:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Ishmael"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Isaac"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Esau"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Joseph"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Isaac was the son of promise born to Abraham and Sarah in old age."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','When God asked Abraham to leave his country, Abraham obeyed. This shows that Abraham had:','[{"id": "a", "text": "fear of animals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "faith and obedience to God"}, {"id": "c", "text": "love for money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hatred for his family"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Leaving his home at God''s word shows Abraham''s faith and obedience."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','When God tested Abraham, He asked him to offer his son on the altar. What did God provide as a substitute?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A ram caught in a bush"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A goat from the market"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A cow from Egypt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A dove from the sky"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "God provided a ram caught in a thicket to be offered instead of Isaac."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','Abraham is often called the ''father of ______'' because of his great trust in God.','[{"id": "a", "text": "faith"}, {"id": "b", "text": "war"}, {"id": "c", "text": "trade"}, {"id": "d", "text": "farming"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Because of his strong trust in God, Abraham is called the father of faith."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','A pupil who obeys his parents and teachers even when it is hard is following the example of Abraham''s:','[{"id": "a", "text": "disobedience"}, {"id": "b", "text": "obedience"}, {"id": "c", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "anger"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Obeying even when difficult reflects Abraham''s obedience to God."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T2','CRS-T2-O2','The main lesson Christians learn from Abraham''s journey is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "trust and obey God completely"}, {"id": "b", "text": "travel to many countries"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gather much wealth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "build tall houses"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Abraham''s life teaches complete trust and obedience to God."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','In which town was Jesus Christ born?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nazareth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Jerusalem"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bethlehem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Egypt"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea."}',0.25,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','What was the name of the mother of Jesus?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Martha"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mary"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Elizabeth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ruth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Mary was the mother of Jesus."}',0.25,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','The angel who announced to Mary that she would give birth to Jesus was:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Michael"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Raphael"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Gabriel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Uriel"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The angel Gabriel announced the birth of Jesus to Mary."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','After Jesus was born, He was laid in a manger because there was no room for them in the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "temple"}, {"id": "b", "text": "inn"}, {"id": "c", "text": "palace"}, {"id": "d", "text": "market"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus was laid in a manger because there was no room in the inn."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O1','The wise men from the East were guided to the baby Jesus by a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "star"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cloud"}, {"id": "c", "text": "river"}, {"id": "d", "text": "map"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A star led the wise men to the place where Jesus was."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','As a boy of twelve, where was Jesus found by His parents after they had been searching for Him?','[{"id": "a", "text": "In the market place"}, {"id": "b", "text": "In the temple with the teachers"}, {"id": "c", "text": "By the river Jordan"}, {"id": "d", "text": "In a garden"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus was found in the temple sitting among the teachers, listening and asking questions."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','The Bible says the boy Jesus grew and became strong, filled with wisdom, and the ______ of God was upon Him.','[{"id": "a", "text": "anger"}, {"id": "b", "text": "grace"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fear"}, {"id": "d", "text": "silence"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The favour, or grace, of God was upon the young Jesus."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','The wise men presented gifts to the baby Jesus. Which of these was one of their gifts?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Silver coins"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Gold"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cloth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bread"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The wise men brought gold, frankincense, and myrrh."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','From the story of the boy Jesus in the temple, Nigerian children learn to be interested in:','[{"id": "a", "text": "learning about God"}, {"id": "b", "text": "playing all day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fighting friends"}, {"id": "d", "text": "eating sweets"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jesus in the temple teaches children to be eager to learn about God."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T3','CRS-T3-O2','The Bible says Jesus went home with His parents and was ______ to them.','[{"id": "a", "text": "rude"}, {"id": "b", "text": "obedient"}, {"id": "c", "text": "unkind"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a stranger"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus was obedient to His parents, setting an example for children."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','At a wedding in Cana, Jesus performed His first miracle by turning water into:','[{"id": "a", "text": "wine"}, {"id": "b", "text": "oil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "honey"}, {"id": "d", "text": "milk"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jesus turned water into wine at the wedding in Cana of Galilee."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','Jesus fed a large crowd of five thousand people using five loaves of bread and:','[{"id": "a", "text": "two fishes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "three eggs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "five oranges"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ten yams"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jesus fed the five thousand with five loaves and two fishes."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','When a great storm arose on the sea, Jesus calmed it by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "rowing the boat quickly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "commanding the wind and waves to be still"}, {"id": "c", "text": "jumping into the water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "calling for more boats"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus rebuked the wind and told the sea to be still, and there was calm."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','The miracles of Jesus show that He has power over:','[{"id": "a", "text": "only human beings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nature, sickness, and death"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only the weather"}, {"id": "d", "text": "only money"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "His miracles reveal His power over nature, sickness, and even death."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O1','Jesus raised His friend Lazarus, who had died, back to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "sleep"}, {"id": "b", "text": "life"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sadness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "prison"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus raised Lazarus from the dead, showing His power over death."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','A short story that Jesus told to teach a spiritual or moral lesson is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "proverb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "parable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "poem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "riddle"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Jesus used parables, which are earthly stories with heavenly meanings."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','In the parable of the Good Samaritan, who helped the wounded man that others had passed by?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A priest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A Levite"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A Samaritan"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A soldier"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The Samaritan showed mercy and cared for the wounded man."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','The main lesson of the parable of the Good Samaritan is that we should:','[{"id": "a", "text": "love and help our neighbours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "travel on lonely roads"}, {"id": "c", "text": "avoid sick people"}, {"id": "d", "text": "keep our money safe"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The parable teaches us to show love and kindness to everyone in need."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','In the parable of the Prodigal Son, how did the father receive his son who returned home?','[{"id": "a", "text": "He sent him away"}, {"id": "b", "text": "He welcomed him with love and forgiveness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "He punished him harshly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "He ignored him"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The father joyfully forgave and welcomed back his lost son."}',0.4,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T4','CRS-T4-O2','The parable of the Prodigal Son teaches Christians about God''s:','[{"id": "a", "text": "anger"}, {"id": "b", "text": "forgiveness and love"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wealth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "silence"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The parable shows God''s great forgiveness and love for repentant sinners."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','Which of these is a good Christian quality that Jesus taught His followers to have?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pride"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Love"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Greed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Jealousy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Love is the chief quality Jesus taught His followers to show."}',0.25,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','Jesus taught that we should forgive those who offend us. This shows the quality of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "forgiveness"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wickedness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "laziness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pride"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Forgiving those who wrong us shows the Christian quality of forgiveness."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','A pupil who always tells the truth and does not cheat in exams is showing:','[{"id": "a", "text": "honesty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hatred"}, {"id": "c", "text": "greed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "anger"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Telling the truth and not cheating shows the good quality of honesty."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','The ''Golden Rule'' that Jesus taught says we should do to others as we would want them to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "do to us"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pay to us"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sell to us"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hide from us"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Golden Rule says to treat others as we would want to be treated."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O1','Sharing your food with a hungry classmate at school shows the Christian quality of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "kindness"}, {"id": "b", "text": "selfishness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rudeness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pride"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sharing with someone in need shows kindness and generosity."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','The prayer that Jesus taught His disciples is commonly called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Lord''s Prayer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Morning Prayer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grace Prayer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Praise Song"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Jesus taught His disciples the Lord''s Prayer, beginning ''Our Father''."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','Prayer is best described as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "talking to and communicating with God"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reading a newspaper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "singing for money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sleeping in church"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Prayer is talking to and communicating with God."}',0.3,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','The Lord''s Prayer begins with the words:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Our Father who art in heaven"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The Lord is my shepherd"}, {"id": "c", "text": "In the beginning God created"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blessed are the poor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Lord''s Prayer opens with ''Our Father who art in heaven''."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','A market trader who gives the correct change and does not use false weights is being:','[{"id": "a", "text": "honest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "greedy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cruel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lazy"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Giving correct change and true measures shows honesty in daily life."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','CRS','CRS-T5','CRS-T5-O2','Why is it important for a Christian child to pray every day?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To stay close to God and receive His guidance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To become richer than others"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To avoid doing homework"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To show off to friends"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Daily prayer keeps a Christian close to God and open to His guidance."}',0.35,'{P5,CRS,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Why should you bath at least twice a day, especially in a hot country like Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To make the body grow taller"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To remove sweat, dirt and body odour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To avoid drinking water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To make clothes last longer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Bathing washes away sweat, dirt and germs that cause body odour."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Which of these is the main reason for brushing your teeth every morning and night?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To prevent tooth decay and bad breath"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To make the mouth bigger"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To help you eat faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To whiten the tongue only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Brushing removes food particles and germs that cause decay and bad breath."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Trimming your fingernails regularly is important because long nails can','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make your fingers stronger"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Help you write neatly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Trap dirt and germs that cause sickness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Make food taste better"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Dirt and germs hide under long nails and can enter the body through food."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Washing your hands with soap and water before eating helps to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make the food sweeter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prevent germs from entering the body"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cool the food quickly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Make your hands soft"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Handwashing removes germs so they are not swallowed with food."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O1','Keeping the hair clean and well combed is part of','[{"id": "a", "text": "Good personal grooming"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cooking practice"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Farm work"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Buying and selling"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Clean, neat hair is part of caring for your appearance and grooming."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','Which tool is best used to clean between the teeth after brushing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Nail cutter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dental floss"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sponge"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Dental floss removes food stuck between the teeth where a brush cannot reach."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','A sponge and soap are mainly used for','[{"id": "a", "text": "Combing the hair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Washing the body during a bath"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cutting the nails"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cleaning the teeth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A sponge with soap scrubs dirt off the skin while bathing."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','The correct tool for cutting overgrown fingernails is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "Toothbrush"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Nail cutter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Towel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Comb"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A nail cutter (clipper) is designed to trim nails safely."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','After a bath, you should dry your body with a clean','[{"id": "a", "text": "Towel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Broom"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Plate"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Comb"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clean towel absorbs water from the skin after bathing."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T1','HEC-T1-O2','It is unhealthy to share which of these grooming items with other people?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A bucket of water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A toothbrush"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A bar of new soap"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A wall mirror"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sharing a toothbrush spreads germs from one person''s mouth to another."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','Which of these Nigerian foods is a good source of carbohydrates for energy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Garri (cassava)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fresh fish"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Groundnut oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ugu leaves"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Garri is a starchy food that gives the body energy."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','Beans, fish and meat are grouped together because they mainly provide','[{"id": "a", "text": "Water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Proteins for growth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fats only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sugar only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "These are body-building foods rich in protein that help the body grow."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','Fruits and vegetables such as orange and ugu are important because they supply','[{"id": "a", "text": "Vitamins and minerals that protect the body"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Only starch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "No nutrients at all"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Fruits and vegetables are protective foods rich in vitamins and minerals."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','Palm oil and groundnut oil belong to which food group?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Proteins"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Vitamins"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fats and oils"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Minerals"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Oils are fats that give the body energy and keep it warm."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O1','A food that helps the body fight and prevent diseases is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "Body-building food"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Energy-giving food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Protective food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cooking food"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Protective foods like fruits and vegetables help the body resist disease."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','A balanced diet is a meal that contains','[{"id": "a", "text": "Only rice and stew"}, {"id": "b", "text": "All the classes of food in the right amounts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only meat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Only fruits"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A balanced diet contains all the food classes in correct proportions."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','Which meal below is the most balanced?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Plain white rice only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Jollof rice with chicken and vegetable salad"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A bottle of soft drink only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Only fried plantain"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "This meal combines carbohydrate, protein and protective foods together."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','Why should you cover cooked food properly before storing it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To keep away flies, dust and germs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To make it change colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To make it heavier"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To make it sweeter"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Covering food protects it from flies, dust and germs that cause spoilage."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','Before cooking, raw vegetables like ugu should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "Left dirty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Washed clean with water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fried without washing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Thrown away"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Washing vegetables removes sand and germs before cooking."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T2','HEC-T2-O2','Perishable foods such as fresh fish and milk are best kept fresh by storing them in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "Refrigerator"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wardrobe"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bookshelf"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Dustbin"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A refrigerator keeps perishable foods cold so they do not spoil quickly."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','Which tool is used to cut fabric neatly when sewing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Scissors"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spoon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Comb"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Broom"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Scissors are used to cut fabric to the required shape and size."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','A thimble is worn on the finger during sewing in order to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make the finger beautiful"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Push the needle without pricking the finger"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Measure the cloth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cut the thread"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A thimble protects the finger while pushing the needle through fabric."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','The stitch used to join two pieces of fabric temporarily before permanent sewing is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tacking (basting) stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cross stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Chain stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blanket stitch"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tacking holds fabric together temporarily before final stitching."}',0.4,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','Which tool is used to measure the length of fabric before cutting?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tape measure"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Needle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Thimble"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Iron"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A tape measure is used to take accurate measurements of fabric."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O1','A needle and thread are used together mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Iron clothes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sew or join fabric"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wash clothes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fold clothes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The needle carries the thread to stitch fabric together."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O2','Why should white clothes be washed separately from coloured clothes?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To make washing take longer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To prevent colours from staining the white clothes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To use more soap"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To tear the clothes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Colours can run and stain white clothes if washed together."}',0.35,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O2','After washing clothes, they are dried best by','[{"id": "a", "text": "Spreading them in the sun or airy place"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keeping them wet in a bucket"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Burying them in the ground"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Folding them while still wet"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sun and fresh air dry clothes and help kill germs."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O2','Ironing a dry cloth is done mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wet the cloth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Remove creases and make it smooth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Change its colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Make it dirty"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ironing removes wrinkles and gives clothes a neat, smooth look."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O2','A torn button on a shirt should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "Ignored"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sewn back or replaced"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cut off completely"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Painted over"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Mending clothes, such as fixing a button, keeps them neat and usable."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T3','HEC-T3-O2','Clean, folded clothes are best kept in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "Kitchen sink"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wardrobe or drawer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dustbin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bathroom floor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A wardrobe or drawer keeps clothes clean, neat and dust-free."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T4','HEC-T4-O1','Which tool is best used to sweep dust and dirt from the floor?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Broom"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Needle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Spoon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pillow"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A broom is used to sweep dirt and dust off the floor."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T4','HEC-T4-O1','To collect the dirt gathered after sweeping, you use a','[{"id": "a", "text": "Dustpan"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bucket of water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Towel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Plate"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A dustpan is used to pack up the swept dirt for disposal."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T4','HEC-T4-O1','A mop and water are mainly used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Comb the hair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wash and clean the floor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cut vegetables"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Iron clothes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A mop with water is used to scrub and clean floors."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T4','HEC-T4-O1','The kitchen should be cleaned regularly mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Attract flies and rats"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keep food and cooking area free of germs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Waste water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Make it dark"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A clean kitchen keeps germs and pests away from food."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T4','HEC-T4-O1','Dusting furniture with a duster helps to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Add more dust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Remove dust and keep it clean"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Break the furniture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Change its colour"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A duster wipes dust from surfaces to keep furniture clean."}',0.25,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
  ('P5','HEC','HEC-T4','HEC-T4-O2','Household refuse should be kept in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "Covered dustbin or waste bin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cooking pot"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wardrobe"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Water tank"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A covered dustbin holds refuse and keeps flies and odour away."}',0.3,'{P5,HEC,CCE,nerdc-quiz-seed-v2}'),
